������ �\n�\n��������� ��������� ��� ��� ������ ��� ����� ���� �� ���� ��� ���� ������ ���������� ��������� �������� ����\n����������� �������� ���������������������� ����� ������ ��������� ����� ����� ������ �������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n�\n������ �\n� ���������������������������������������������������������������� �\n� �\n���� � ����� � ������ ���������� � �� � �������� ����� �\n�������\n���������� �� � �� � �������������� �����\n�������\n��������� � ������\n���������� � ����� ���� � ���� � � � ���� � � ���� �����\n���������� �� ���� ����� �� ���� �� ���� �� ����� ��� �� � �����\n���������� ��� ���� �� �� �� �� �� �� ���� ����� �� � �����\n���������� �� �� �� �� �� �� �� �� �� �� �� � ��\n���������� �� ���� �� ��� ��� �� ��� �� �� �� ��� � ����\n���������� �� ��� �� �� �� �� �� ���� �� ����� �� � �����\n������ � � � � � � � � � � � � ������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |224", "t": "Implementation of NCLP", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 224 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF NCLP \n \n224.  SHRI SUDHAKAR TUKARAM SHRANGARE: \n  SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA:  \nSHRI DIPSINH SHANKARSINH RATHOD:  \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a)the number of districts in which the National Child Labour Project \n(NCLP) is being implemented, Statewise specially in Maharashtra \nand Gujarat; \n(b)the e xtent to which the implementation of NCLP has been \nsuccessful during last Ten years; and  \n(c)the fresh steps taken by the Government to provide education to \nthe children of the families engaged in various industries near the \nplace of their residence? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a): The number of districts in which the National Child Labour \nProject (NCLP) Scheme has been sanctioned on the basis of proposals \nreceived from the State Government/ District Administration and is \ncurrently operational is annexed.  \n \n(b):  6,80,528 number of children were rescued/ withdrawn from work, \nrehabilitated and mainstreamed under NCLP Scheme during 2011-12 to \n2020-21.  \nContd..2/- \n\n:: 2 :: \n(c): Under Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan  (SSA) Scheme, special training \nfor age appropriate admission of out of school children and residential \nas well as non -residential training for o lder children, seasonal hostels / \nresidential camps, special training centres at worksites, transport/ \nescort facility are also supported to bring out of school children to the \nformal schooling system. Also, mid -day meal is provided to the \nstudents at the elementary level of education. \n \n*                                                      ******** \n  \n\n�������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������� ���������������������������\n��������� ���� ���� ���� ����������� � � ��� � ����� ��������� ��������\n���������� � ��� �� ���������� ��������� ����������� ����� ��������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������� ���\n�\n������� ��� ����� � ������ ������������������������� ���������� ���� ��� �����\n����������� �\n�\n����\n����\n�������������� �����������������������\n����������\n������������������������������\n�����������\n��� � ��������������� ��� ��\n��� � ����� � �� ��\n��� � ������ ��� ��\n��� � ������������� �� ��\n��� � �������� �� ��\n��� � �������� �� ��\n��� � ���������������� �� ��\n��� � ���������� �� ��\n��� � ���������� ��� ��\n����� ��������������� ��� ��\n����� ������������ ��� ��\n����� ���������� �� ��\n����� ������� ��� ��\n����� ������� �� ��\n����� ���������� ��� ��\n����� ����������� ��� ���\n����� ���������� ��� ��\n����� �������������� ��� ��\n����� ������������ ��� ��\n����� ������������ ��� ��\n����� ������ �� ��\n� ������ ����� ���\n��������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |225", "t": "Requirement of Banks", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO\n. \n225\n \nTO BE ANSWER ON THE \n1\n4\nTH\nDECEMBER\n, 2021  \n \nCROP DIVERSIFICATION\n \n*\n225\n.\n \nSHRI\n \nSUSHIL KUMAR SINGH\n:\n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n(\na\n)\n \nthe details of steps being taken by the Government to promote crop diversification\n; \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nwhether the Government has tried to gauge the quantifiable impact o\nf these steps\n;\n \n(\nc\n)\n \nif so, the details thereof\n \nand if not, the reasons therefor;\n \n(\nd\n)\n \nthe list of perceived benefits of crop diversification\n; and\n \n(\ne\n)\n \nthe list of best practices being implemented by different State Governments\n \nto \npromote crop diversification\n?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NAREN\nDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n(a) to (e\n):\n      \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n225\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON 14.12.2021 REGARDING “CROP \nDIVERSIFICATION”\n.\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nto (c)\n:\n \nThe Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare (DA&FW) is implementing \nthe Crop Diversification Programme (CDP), a sub\n-\nscheme of Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana \n(RKVY) in the Origina\nl Green Revolution States viz; Haryana, Punjab & Western Uttar \nPradesh since 2013\n-\n14 to divert the area of water intensive paddy crop to alternative crops \nlike pulses, oilseeds, coarse cereals, nutri cereals, cotton etc. \nCDP was extended to \ndiversifying to\nbacco crop in 10 tobacco growing states of Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Gujarat, \nKarnataka, Maharashtra, Odisha, Tamil Nadu, Telangana, Uttar Pradesh and West Bengal \nfrom 2015\n-\n16. \nUnder CDP assistance is \ngiven \nfor \nalternative\n \ncrops demonstration, farm \nmechanization and value addition, site specific activities and contingency for awareness \nand capacity building. \nCDP aims at demonstrating alternative crops at farmers field and the \narea brought under demonstrations \nis \n6.32\n \nlakh h\nectare during 2013\n-\n14 to 2020\n-\n21.\n \n \n \n \n \nIn addition, Government of India is also supplementing the efforts of state \ngovernments to encourage diversified production of crops such as pulses, coarse cereals, \nnutri cereals, cotton & oilseeds under National Food \nSecurity Mission (NFSM) and \nhorticultural crops under Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH). \nGovernment of India also provide flexibility to the states for state specific needs/priorities \nunder RKVY. The state can promote crop diversifi\ncation under RKVY with the approval of \nState Level Sanctioning Committee (SLSC) headed by Chief Secretary of the State\n.\n \n \n(d)\n:\n    \nThe diversification towards alternative crops to paddy are more beneficial for \nsustain\nable agriculture which promote\n \nyield\n,\n \nless amount of resources like water, nutrient \netc besides protection to soil and environment\n \nby growing alternative crops\n.\n \n \n\n \n(e)\n:\n \nThe Government of India conduct demonstration\ns\n \non various crops at farmers field \nthrough Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs), State A\ngricultural Universities \n(SAUs) \nand ICAR\n-\n \nnetwork. \nBesides\n, t\nhe States adopt different strategies\n \nfor existing pattern of crops, \nas per \nthe priority of the State Government. \nICAR\n-\nCentral Research Institute for Dryland \nAgriculture (CRIDA) also suggest \nthe alternative cropping system \nto \nstates.\n \n*********\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |226", "t": "Encroachment of Hindu Temples in South India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.226 \nANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 \n \n \nENCROACHMENT OF HINDU TEMPLES IN SOUTH INDIA \n \n†226. SHRI ANURAG SHARMA:  \n \n           Will the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a) the number of Hindu temples are registered in South India and out of these the \nnumber of temples that are under the Government admini stration and private \nmanagement; \n(b) the details of those Hindu temples that are under encroachment in above both \ncategory; \n(c) the details of the instructions given by the Government of India to the State \nGovernments to remove the encroachments from the temples in South India; \nand \n(d) whether these instructions have been followed and if not, the  reason therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF CULTURE, TOURISM \nAND DEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN REGION \n \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n       (a) There are 1097 monuments and sites which  have been declared as Centrally \nProtected  in the State of Andhra Pradesh (135), Karnataka (506), Kerala (29) , \nPudduchery- UT (07), Tamil Nadu (412) and Telangana (08). Out of these 448 are \nTemples. \n     (b) The details of temples where encroachments reported are at Annexure. \n (c) & (d) Wherever encroachment is reported, notice is given to the defaulter to remove the \nsame; failing which, Demolition Order is issued as per provisions of the Ancient \nMonuments and Archaeological Sites and Remains Act,1958 with request to \nCommissioner or Collector to cause demolition of the encroachment.  Sometimes \nlitigations in various courts also cause delay in removal of encroachments.     \n \n  \n\nAnnexure \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF  LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 226 FOR 29.11.2021 \n \nSl. \nNo. \nName of Monument \n(Temple) \n \nLocality District State \n1 Gowrishwara Temple Yelandur Camarajanagar Karnataka \n \n2 Virupaksha Temple Hampi Ballary Karnataka \n \n3 Dhenuipuriswara Temple  Madambakkam  Kanchipurma  Tamil Nadu \n \n4 Siva (Erumbeswaraswami) \nTemple  \nTiruverumbur Tiruchchirapalli Tamil Nadu  \n5 Large Siva Temple \n(Apathsahayeswara Temple) \nThenneri  Kanchipuram Tamil Nadu \n6 Airavateswara Temple  Chattram-\nDarasuram \nThanjavur  Tamil Nadu \n \n***** \n  \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |227", "t": "Non-payment of Wages", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO\n. \n2\n2\n7\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n1\n4\nTH\n \nDECEMBER\n, 2021\n \n \nCULTIVATION OF MILLETS\n \n \n*\n2\n2\n7\n.  \nDR. ARVIND KUMAR SHARMA\n:\n \n           \nSHRI AJAY NISHAD\n:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe details of production of millets \nduring each of the \nlast three years and current year, \nState/UT\n-\nwise\n;\n \n \n(b)\n \nwhether the Government is making efforts or considering to improve cultivation \nacreage and minimum support price for millets as \nit is a\n \nvery important source of nutrition for \npoor farmers and \nis\n \nalso very resource efficient\n;\n \n \n(c)\n \nif so, the details thereof\n \nand the achievements made so far; and\n \n \n(d\n)\n \nif not\n, the \nreasons therefor\n?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n             \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (d):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. \n227\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n14\nTH\n \nDECEMBER\n, 2021.\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \nThe details of \nstate\n-\nwise \nproduction of nutri\n-\ncereals (millets) during last three years & \ncurrent year is given at \nAnnexure\n. \n \n \n(b) to (d\n)\n:\n \nDepartment of Agriculture \nand Farmers \nWelfare (DA&FW) \nis implementing a \nSub\n-\nMission on Nutri\n-\nCereals (Millets) under National Food Security Mission (NFSM) since \n2018\n-\n19\n \nto increase area, \nproduction & productivity\n \nof millets \nin 212 \ndistricts of 14 States\n. \nThe North Eastern States, Himachal Pradesh an\nd UT\ns\n \nof Jammu & Kashmir and Lad\nak\nh\n \nhave \nbeen \ngiven flexibility to \ninclude the districts under \nprogramme on nutri\n-\ncereals\n.\n \nRelease\n \n(central share) \nmade \nto the states \nunder NFSM\n-\nNutri\n \nCereals \nprogramme \nduring last three \nyears & current year is as under:\n \n                                                                                                                       \n(Rs. in crores)\n \nYear\n \nRelease\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n73.38\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n99.03\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n99.57\n \n2021\n-\n22\n*\n \n43.71\n \n \n*As on 06/12/21\n \n \n \nIn view of health benefits of millets, the Government of India notified millets as nutri\n-\n \ncereals in April, 2018. Nutri\n-\ncereals contribute substantially for food & nutritional security and \nare highly \nnutritious. Millet crops perform well in marginal (dryland) environments and are \nsuperior in nutritional properties with high micronutrient with low glycemic indices. Millets are \nnot only comparable to major cereals with respect to their nutritional featur\nes but are very \ngood sources of carbohydrates, micronutrients & phytochemicals with nutraceutical \nproperties. Millets are natural source of iron, zinc, calcium & other nutrients.\n \n \n \nT\nhe production of millets has increased from 137.11 lakh tonnes in 2018\n-\n19 \nto 179.59 \nlakh tonnes in 2020\n-\n21. To encourage the farmers to grow nutri\n-\ncereals (millets), \nGovernment declares Minimum Support Price (MSP) of three major millets i.e, \njowar, bajra & \nragi \nalong \nwith a \n  \nminimum return of at least \n50 per cent over all India\n \nweighted average cost \n \n\