n of railway line \nbetween Bairabi and Sairang under Northeast Frontier Railway \n(NFR); \n \n(b) the total project cost and the expenditure incurred so far on the \nproject; \n \n(c) the length of the railway line under constructio n and the details \nregarding number of bridges, tunnels and stations to be built; and  \n \n(d) the benefits that are likely to accrue to the local population in \nterms of employment generation, passenger movement and \ncarriage of goods? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 241 BY SHRI C. LALROSANGA TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 15.12.2021 REGARDING BAIRABI-SAIRANG RAILWAY LINE \n \n \n(a) to (d): Indian Railways have taken up construction of Bhairabi - Sairang \n(51.38 km) New Line project.  Anticipated cost of the project is  `6527 crore. \nSo far, an expenditure of `4343 crore has been incurred on the project. An \noutlay of `1038 crore has been provided for the financial year 2021 -22 for \nthe project.  \n \nThe length of the railway line under construction is 51.38 km. Project \ninvolves construction of 55 major bridges having total length of 10.68 km, \n87 minor bridges, 32 tunnels of total length 12.65 km  and 5 station \nbuildings. Proposed stations are Bairabi (existing), Hortoki, Kawnpui, \nMaulkhang and Sairang - terminal station. \n \nThe completion of any Railway project depends on various factors like \nquick land acquisition by State Government, forest clearance by officials of \nforest department, shifting of infringing utilities, statutory clearances from \nvarious authorities, geological and topographic al conditions of area, law \nand order situation in the area of project site , etc.  All these factors affect \nthe completion time of the project.  As such, confirmed completion time of \nproject cannot be ascertained. Nevertheless, every effort is being made to  \nexecute the project expeditiously. \n \n This is a National Project and improving connectivity in isolated \nportions of North East is a Government of India policy initiative.  \nEmployment generation opportunities have already grown due to ongoing \nlarge-scale construction activities in North Eastern Region. Social and \neconomic development will follow as a consequence of improved \nconnectivity with rest of the country. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |242", "t": "Share of States in Crop Insurance Scheme", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 242 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 15.12.2021 \n \nEXTENSION OF RAILWAY LINE FROM KARIMGANJ TO ZAMUANG \n \n*242. SHRI KRIPANATH MALLAH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware about the long pending public \ndemand for extension of Baraigram -Anipur-Dullavcherra railway \nline in Karimganj district of Assam to Zamuang in Mizoram to \nboost inter-state rail connectivity and to enable socio -economic \ndevelopment in the remote areas of Assam-Mizoram border; \n \n(b) whether the Government will consider to include the said \nproposal in the upcoming Budget for the year 2022-23; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 242 BY SHRI KRIPANATH MALLAH TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 15.12.2021 REGARDING EXTENSION \nOF RAILWAY LINE FROM KARIMGANJ TO ZAMUANG \n \n \n(a) to (c):    Interstate rail connectivity between Assam and Mizoram \nis already available as railway line from Katakhal in Assam to \nBhairabi in Mizoram already exists.  Further, Bhairabi to Sairang \nrailway line in Mizoram is also sanctioned. Bhairabi – Sairang is a \ncapital connectivity project and will furthe r provide connectivity to \nremote areas of Mizoram. Zamuang is only 29 km from Sairang. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |243", "t": "Improving Status of Transgender Population", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nI{llNtsTRY OF GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DTSTRTBUTION\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTIOil\n\\ .oKsaBHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.243\nTO BE ANSWERED ON {srH DECEMBERT 2O2{\n*243. DR. SUJAV RADHAKRISHI{A VIKHE PATTL:\nSHRI U]{IVI ESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL:\nWlll the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND pUBLIc\nDISTRIBUTTON Ecgtfir arri, uf-c git{ €rffi*, fuilq f+ be pteased to\nstate:\n(a) whether the Government is imptementing interest subvention\nscheme for civil supplies for Ethano! Plants;\n(b) if so, the details of the funds allocated, sanctioned and disburced\nduring the last three yearc for the purpose, State/Union Territory-wise,\nspecially to the State of Maharashtra;\n(c)\nand\nthe details of Letter of lntent that have been issued by the Ministry;\n(d) the number of persons who have been benefited under the scheme,\nState/Union Territory.wise, specially in the State of Maharashtra?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF GOMMERGE & INDUSTRY, cor{suMER AFFATRS, FOOD &\nPUBLIG DISTRIBUTION AND TEXTILES\n(sHR! PTYUSH GOYAL)\nSUPPLIES FOR ETHANOL PLANT\n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |244", "t": "Artificial Insemination of Dairy Animals and Bovines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 244 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 15.12.2021 \n \nRAIL CONNECTIVITY IN TRIBAL DOMINATED AREAS \n \n†*244.  SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of  the tribal dominated district headquarters in the \ncountry, especially in Maharashtra, that are yet to be connected \nwith rail network; \n \n(b) whether the Union Government has taken/proposes to take steps \nto connect these tribal -dominated district headquarter s with rail \nnetwork; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 244 BY SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE           \nTO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 15.12.2021 REGARDING RAIL  \nCONNECTIVITY IN TRIBAL DOMINATED AREAS \n \n(a) to (d): The Railway projects are sanctioned Zonal Railway wise \nand not State -wise, District wise or area wise as the Rail ways’ \nprojects may span across S tate boundaries. S anction of new railway \nlines in areas which are not connected by Railway network including \ntribal dominated areas is a continuous and ongoing p rocess of Indian \nRailways. \n \nAs on 01.04.2021, Indian Railways has taken up 187 New line projects \nof 21,037 km length, costing `4,05,916 crore, which are in various \nstages of planning/approval/execution, out of which commissioning of \n2,621 km length has bee n achieved and expenditure of `1,05,591 crore \nhas been incurred upto March, 2021. These new line projects will \nprovide connectivity to areas which are not connected with Railway \nnetwork including tribal dominated areas. \n \nMost of the tribal dominated distri ct headquarters of Maharashtra \nnamely Nandurbar, Dhule, Nasik and Palghar are already connected on \nrailway network. Railway has also taken up Wadsa – Gadchiroli new \nline project for connecting Gadchiroli, which is one of the tribal \ndominated district headquarter. \n \n..P/2  \n\n-:2:- \nAs on 01.04.2021, 16 New Line Projects costing `49,221 crore for 2,017 \nkm length falling fully/partly in Maharashtra are under differen t stages \nof planning/ approval/ execution, out of which 62 km length has been \ncommissioned and an e xpenditure of  `4,563 crore has been incurred \nupto March, 2021.  \n \nDetails of all ongoing Railway projects including cost, expenditure and \noutlay are made available in public domain on Indian Railways website \ni.e. www.indianrailways.gov.in >Ministry of Railways >Railway Board \n>About Indian Railways >Railway Board Directorates >Finance \n(Budget) >Rail Budget/Pink Book (Year)> Railway wise Works \nMachinery and Rolling Stock Programme. \n \nDuring 2014-21, 17720 km projects (3681 km of New Line, 4871 km of \nGauge Conversion and 9168 km of Doubling) have been commissioned \nin the country at an average rate 2531.5 km per year, which is 66% \nmore than average commissioning during 2009-14 (1520 km/year). \n \nDuring 2014 -21, 916 km section (87 km New Line, 136 km Gauge \nConversion and 693 km Doubling) falling fully/partly in the State of \nMaharashtra have been commissioned at an average rate 130.86 km \nper year, which is 124% more than average annual commissioning \nduring 2009-14 (58.4 km/year). \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |245", "t": "Garima Greh for Transgenders", "head": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) \n \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 245 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 15th DECEMBER, 2021 \n \n \nINDO-US TRADE RELATIONS \n \n *245.  SHRI SUDHEER GUPTA: \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY  (वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्री ) be \npleased to state: \n \n(a) whether USA has lifted or is considering to lift the ban on entry of Indian fruits to American \nmarkets and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) whether this welcome step will resolve the outstanding trade issues between the two countries \nand if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the USA and Indian Governments have formed any trade policy forum for regular \ninteraction with each other and if so, the details thereof; \n(d) the steps taken by the Government for registration of packing houses and processing units for \nfresh fruits and vegetables to ensure compliance with international standards;  \n(e) whether ban on certain vegetables like bitter gourd, eggplant, etc., is still continuing and if so, \nthe details thereof and the efforts made for lifting of the ban on these vegetables; and  \n(f) the amount of revenue likely to be generated from exports after lifting of the ban? \n \nANSWER \nokf.kT; ,oa m|ksx ea=h ( Jh ih;w’k xks;y ) \n \nTHE MINISTER OF  COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY  \n (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)  \n  \n(a) to (f):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****  \n\n2 \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT  REFERRED  TO  IN  REPLY  TO  PARTS  (a) to (f)  OF  LOK  SABHA  \nSTARRED  QUESTION  NO. 245   FOR  ANSWER  ON  15th DECEMBER, 2021   \nREGARDING   “ INDO-US TRADE RELATIONS”. \n \n \n(a) and (b):   There is no ban on entry of Indian fruits into the U.S. market. India has market \naccess for fruits including banana, pomegranate, mango, watermelon and coconut. \nHowever, the export of pomegranate arils was suspended by the U.S. in 2018. Further, the \nexport of Indian mangoes and pomegranate fruits was held up since 2020 in the wake of \nCOVID-19 pandemic as export pre-clearance inspection by the US inspectors could not be \ncarried out due to  travel restrictions.  \nIn the 12 th India-US Trade Policy Forum Meeting  held on 23 rd November 2021,the U.S. \nagreed to finalize market access for pomegranate arils as well as oversight transfer to India \nfor pre -clearance for mangoes and pomegranate, which will facilitate export of these \ncommodities to the U.S. \n(c):      The India-U.S. Trade Policy Forum (TPF),formed in 2005, is a bilateral forum for \ndiscussion and resolution of trade and investment issues between the two countries. It is co-\nchaired by Indian Commerce & Industry Minister and the United States Trade \nRepresentative. The 12 th India-U.S. TPF Ministerial meeting was convened on \n23rd November, 2021. After the meeting a Joint Statement covering the ambit of bilateral \ntrade and commercial issues and way forward was released, which   is available at \nhttps://commerce.gov.in/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/TPF-Joint-Statement-2021-Nov-23-\nFinal.pdf.  \n \n(d):        To ensure compliance with international s tandards for fruits and vegetables and \nother horticulture produce, Government provides grant for setting up of pack houses. In \naddition, Government bodies viz APEDA (Agricultural and Processed Food Products Export \nDevelopment Authority) and NPPO (National Plant Protection Organization) register and \nrecognize pack houses based on the Standard Operating Procedure in conformity with \nestablished international standards such as International Organization for Standardization \n(ISO)/Hazard Analysis Critical Control Points (HACCP)/ British Retail Consortium (BRC). \n(e) and (f): There is no ban on entry of vegetables such as bitter gourd and eggplants from \nIndia to the U.S. As per  DGCIS figures, India exported US$ 72.57 million worth of vegetables \nin 2019-20 and US$ 101.25 million in 2020-21 to the US. \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |246", "t": "Crop Damage due to Climate Change", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.246 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 15.12.2021 \n \n‘BHAVINI’ FAST BREEDER REACTOR \n \n*246. SHRI VINCENT H.PALA:  \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether India’s first 500 MW Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor ‘BHAVINI’ has \nbeen commissioned in its entirety and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b)  whether the project has suffered time overruns and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)      the estimated cost overruns of the project; and \n \n(d)  whether the Government has invested in other  similar projects and if so, the \ndetails of their status and estimated time of completion? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES & \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (DR.JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a)to(d)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nGovernment of India \nDepartment of Atomic Energy \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. *246 FOR ANSWER ON 15.12.2021 BY SHRI VINCENT H. PALA \nREGARDING ‘BHAVINI’ FAST BREEDER REACTOR. \n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ \n \n \n(a)  No, Sir. The 500 MWe Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor (PFBR) being built by  \nBharatiya Nabhikiya Vidyut Nigam Limited ( BHAVINI) at Kalpakkam is under \nintegrated commissioning stage. \n \n(b)  Yes, Sir. The Project is originally sanctioned in 2003 and expected completion \nwas by September 2010. According to latest approval , the revised completion \ntarget for the project is October 2022. \n \n(c)   The project was originally sanctioned in 2003 at a cost of Rs . 3492 crore. The \ncost was further revised to Rs . 5667 crores subsequently.  Government has \napproved the revised completion cost of Rs. 6840 crore in 2021. \n \n(d) Government has allocated Rs. 250 crore for the pre -project activities of Fast \nBreeder Reactor (FBR) -1&2 to be built at Kalpakkam. The pre -project \nactivities are under progress. Detailed design & analyses of FBR -1&2 are \nunder progress in Indira Gandhi Cent re for Atomic Research (IGCAR) taking \ninto consideration the commissioning & operational feedback of PFBR. The \nproject is yet to be sanctioned. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |247", "t": "Grants from Finance Commission", "head": "STATEMENT REFERRED To lN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF THE\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.247 DUE FOR ANSYUER ON {5.,I2.202{ IN THE\nLOK SABHA.\n(a) & (b): As per guidelines for allocation, distribution and disposal of\ncoarse grains, States are allowed to procure coarse grain (Jowar,\nBaira, Maize & Ragi etc.) from f,armers at Minimum Support price\n(MSP) under centra! pool with the prior approvat of Government of\nlndia. The procured quantity has to be distributed under Targeted\nPublic Distribution,System (TPDS)/Other Welfare Schemes (OWS) in the\nI\nStates/UTs and thle combined atlocation of wheat and rice to the\nequivalent quantity of coanBe grains shall stand automatically reduced.\nGovernment Jof lndia permits procurement bf those coanse\ngrains/millets for which llllSP is declared on the basis of the\nrecommendations of the Gommission for Agricultural Gosts and Prices\n(GACP) to ensure remunetative price of produce to farmerc. Presenfly,\nmillets like Jowar, Baira and Ragi are covered under MSP. Government\nof lndia has not received any piocurement proposal for procurement of\nMinor Millet Rice from any State Government.\n\nprovide that the RLBs’ accounts for various financial transactions out of Fifteenth Finance \nCommission Grants are to be carried out on eGramSwaraj -PFMS Interface. The annual audit \nof the accounts of the RLBs ar e required to be carried out through AuditOnline  Application. \nThese mechanisms would facilitate monitoring the release and expenditure of the grants.  \n(c) The Operational Guidelines dated 14.07.2021 of Ministry of Finance has prescribed the \ndistribution criteria in accordance with recommendations of FC-XV for the RLBs to all the \nTiers in the Panchayats i.e. Gram Panchayats, Block/Taluk  Panchayats and District/Zila  \nPanchayats and to areas which are not required to have Panchayats (Sixth Schedule Areas and \nExcluded Areas). The inter se distribution among all the tiers shall be done by the concerned \nState Government on the basis of accepted recommendations of the latest State Finance \nCommission (SFC) and in conformity with the bands prescribed by FC-XV.  However, in the \nevent of SFC recommendations not being available, the inter se distribution among all the tiers \nshall be decided by the concerned State Government within the bands prescribed by FC-XV. \nOnce the State-level grants are earmarked for each tier, the intra -tier distribution among the \nrelevant entities across the State shall be on the basis of population (as per Census 2011) and \narea in the ratio of 90:10 or as per the accepted recommendations of the latest SFC. After \nfinalizing the distribution criteria, the States have to release the FC-XV grants to the concerned \nentities (Gram Panchayats/Block Panchayats/Zila  Panchayats and Excluded Areas, if any) as \nper the distribution criteria without any dis cretion for increasing and decreasing such grants. \nThe States are required to certify in their respective GTCs submitted that the Grant distribution \nis as per Census 2011 population or as per the SFC recommendations.  \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |248", "t": "Soil Health Card Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.248 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 15.12.2021 \n \nROB/RUB IN TELANGANA \n *248.    SHRI PASUNOORI DAYAKAR: \n          DR. G. RANJITH REDDY: \n        \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is true that 69 proposals for construction of \nROBs/RUBs at level crossings have been received in the Ministry \nfrom Government of Telangana during the last three years and if \nso, the details thereof, district-wise; \n(b) whether it is true that only 22  ROBs/RUBs have been sanctioned \nby the Ministry; \n(c) if so, the current status of the remaining ROBs/ RUBs; \n(d) the status of the 22 approved projects and by when these are \nlikely to be completed; \n(e) whether the Ministry is contemplating to produce/ manufacture \nLHB Coaches which are cheap and can be completed in a short \nperiod of time; and  \n(f) if so, the details in this regard? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n(a) to (f): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 248  BY SHRI PASUNOORI DAYAKAR AND \nDR. G. RANJITH REDDY  TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n15.12.2021 REGARDING ROB/RUB IN TELANGANA \n \n(a) to (d): Yes, Sir.  69 proposals were received by Zonal Railway from \nGovernment of Telangana between 2018 -19 to 2021 -22, in which 24 \nproposals were repeated.  Thus, only 45 actual proposals have been \nreceived during this period.  Out of 45, 27 valid proposals  have been \nsanctioned by Railways.  3 Road Under Bridges (RUBs)  have already \nbeen completed and balance Road Over Bridges (ROB )/ RUB are in \ndifferent stages of planning, design and development.  Construction of \nROB/RUBs depends upon the consent of State G overnment for closure \nof Level Crossings (LCs) and cost sharing, wherever applicable, \navailability of encroachment free land for approach roads, technical \nfeasibility, shifting of utilities, allocation of adequate funds by State \nagencies, public support et c. Therefore, it is not feasible to fix \ntimelines for completion of these ROB/RUBs.  District-wise details and \nthe status of these ROBs/RUBs is appended.    \nProposals for construction of Road Over Bridge/Road Under  \nBridge (ROB/RUB) in lieu of Level Crossings (LCs) are either \nconceptualized by Zonal Railways or received from State Government \nand other Statutory Authorities.  Regarding balance 18 proposals, \nvarious aspects are in discussion with State Government/Statu tory \nAuthorities regarding the consent for sharing of cost, approval of \nconcept profile sketch, closure of LC etc. and proposals are yet to be \nfirmed up.   \n  \n\n(e) & (f): With a view to provide safer and more comfortable journey to \nthe travelling passengers, it has inter-alia been decided to proliferate / \ninduct Linke Hofmann Busch (LHB) coaches. In this context, trains \noperating with conventional Integral Coach Factory (ICF) type coaches \nare replaced by LHB coaches, in a phased manner. LHB coaches are \ntechnologically superior and have better riding, aesthetics and safety \nfeatures than conventional ICF type coaches. To this end, Production \nUnits of Indian Railways are producing only LHB coaches from 2018 -19 \nonwards. \n****** \n  \n\nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PA RTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 248  BY SHRI PASUNOORI DAYAKAR AND DR. G. RANJITH \nREDDY  TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 15.12.2021 REGAR DING \nROB/RUB IN TELANGANA \n \n(a) to (d): Details of proposals for sanctioned  ROB/RUB are as follows. \nSN Division Major \nSection \nLC \nNo. \nDistrict ROB/\nRUB \nStatus \n1 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n239 Medak RUB RUB sanctioned in \n2018-19. Work \ncompleted.  \n2 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-Dhone \n7 Rangareddy ROB ROB sanctioned in \n2018-19. Railway \nportion and one side \ncompleted. Other side \napproach work held up \nfor want of Land \nacquisition by State \nGovernment. \n3 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-Dhone \n27 Mahabubnag\nar \nROB Work sanctioned in \n2018-19, Estimate for \napproaches awaited \nfrom State \nGovernment. \n4 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-Dhone \n90A Wanaparthi ROB ROB sanctioned in \n2019-20. Works are in \ndifferent stages of \nplanning, design & \ndevelopment.   \n5 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n250 Medchal-\nMalkajgiri \nROB \n6 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n2/MLY Medchal-\nMalkajgiri \nROB \n7 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n209 A Kamareddy ROB \n8 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n12/JB Nizamabad ROB \n9 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n18/JB Nizamabad ROB \n\n10 Hyderabad Secundera\nbad-\nMudkhed \n228 Medak ROB \n11 Secunderab\nad \nKazipet-\nVijayawada \n110 Khammam RUB,\nROB \nROB with RUB \nsanctioned in 2019 -20. \nRUB completed. \nAlignment to be \nfinalized by State \nGovernment for ROB.   \n12 Secunderab\nad \nBallharsha-\nKazipet \n6 Warangal ROB ROB sanctioned in \n2020-21. Alignment to \nbe finalized by State \nGovernment.   \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n13 Secunderab\nad \nBallh"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |249", "t": "Fish Production in Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh", "head": "1 \n \n������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�������������� ����� �\n�\n��������� �\n��������������������� ����\n�������������������� ��� �������������� �\n�\n� �������������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������������ �\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������\n�\n����� �������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n���������������������������������������� �\n�������������������������������������� �\n����������������������� �\n�\n����������� ������������������������������������������������\n� �\n\n2 \n \n��������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���������� ��������������������������������������������� ��������\n���� ��������������������� ���������� �������������������� ��� ���������� ��������� ��� ������\n���� ���\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n��� ���������������������������������������������������������\n���� �������������������������������������������������������\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� �������������������������������� ������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���������� ���� ��������� ��� ����������� ���� ����������� ��� ����������������� ������\n���������������������������������\n���� �������� ��� ��� ������ ��������� �������� ��� �