 \u0000H\u0000D\u0000U\u0000P\u0000D\u0000U\u0000N\u0000H\u0000G\u0000\u0003\n\u0000I\u0000R\u0000U\u0000\u0003 \u0000J\u0000L\u0000U\u0000O\u0000\u0003 \u0000V\u0000W\u0000X\u0000G\u0000H\u0000Q\u0000W\u0000V\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0003 \u00007\u0000K\u0000"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |27", "t": "Capacity Building in Green Finance", "head": "Government of India \nMinistry of Finance \nDepartment of Economic Affairs \n \nLOK SABHA Unstarred QUESTION NO.27 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 29TH NOVEMBER, 2021/SRAVANA 18, 1943 \n(SAKA) Capacity Building in Green Finance \n \n27. SHRI ARVIND DHARMAPURI: \n \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n(a) Whether the Government has taken any initiatives for capacity building in Green \nFinance during the last five years ; \n(b) if so the details thereof; and \n(c) the details of the partnerships with private companies and the Government for sustainable \nmobility in the last ten years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FINANCE (SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) &(b). Yes, sir. The initiatives taken by the Government, financial sector regulators  and \ngovernment agencies for building capacity in Green Finance in recent past are as under: \ni. The Centre for Advanced Financial Research and Learning (CAFRAL) promoted by the \nReserve Bank of India organized a Conference on Green and Sustainable Finance in \nSeptember 2021 for banks, financial institutions and NBFCs dealing with green finance. It \nhad also organised a Program on Agro-MSE Lending in September 2020. \nii. Indian Renewable Energy Development Agency Limited (IREDA), in association with \nInternational Solar Alliance (ISA), sponsored eight virtual training programme for bankers \nin ISA Member countries. The training programme s were organized by Skill Council of \nGreen Jobs, New Delhi. \n(c). Under a Technical Assistance program from the A sian Development Bank , NITI Aayog is \nworking with the project partners on Pr omoting Clean Energy Usage through Enhanced \nAdoption of Electric Vehicles and Grid Integration of Battery Energy Storage Systems. \nMoreover, IREDA intends to finance projects to tap the emerging market segment of Electric \nVehicle (EV) and EV infrastructure.   \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |270", "t": "Negative Net Balance Sheet under MGNREGS", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 270 \nANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 \n \nSOLAR PROJECTS IN ODISHA \n \n*270. SHRIMATI SARMISTHA SETHI \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) The details of ongoing solar projects in the State of Odisha, particularly in Jajpur \ndistrict.  \n(b) The expenditure incurred on the said projects; and  \n(c) The status of work done/being done in this regard in Jajpur district.  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) to(c) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 270 (10TH POSITION) FOR 16.12.2021 REGARDING SOLAR PROJECTS IN \nODISHA \n(a) Government of Odisha has reported that 653 solar plants with total capacity of 6910.69  \nKW  have been taken up by Orissa Renewable Energy Development Agenc y (OREDA) for \nsolarization of Fire Stations, Panchayat Samiti Offices, Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas, \nOdisha Aadarsha Vidyalayas, Health Institutions and of Mines under Odisha Mining \nCorporation. Against this, 21 solar plants of capacity 385 KW are in Jajpur District. Out of \nthese, three have been completed (all three in Jajpur) and others are under implementation.  \nThe details of these plants in the State of Odisha including those in Jajpur district are given in \nAnnexure-I. \n \n(b) Government of Odisha has reported that expenditure of Rs. 17.29 Crore has been incurred \non solarization of the Fire Stations, Panchayat Samiti Offices, Kasturba Gandhi Balika \nVidyalayas, Odisha Aadarsha Vidyalayas, Health Institutions and of Mines unde r Odisha \nMining Corporation. Against this, expenditure of Rs. 0.65 Crore has been incurred in Jajpur \nDistrict.  The details are given in Annexure-II. \n(c) The three completed plants are in Jajpur district. The other plants out of 653 taken up are \nunder implementation. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a)  of LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 270 FOR 16.12.2021 \nDETAILS OF SOLAR PLANTS IN ODISHA AND JAJPUR DISTRICT: \nSl. \nNo \nName of the Project State Jajpur \n(out of total in State)  \nNo. of \nPlants \nCumulative \nCapacity (In \nKW)  \nNo. of  \nPlants  \nCumulative \nCapacity  (In \nKW) \n1 Solarization of Fire \nStations \n313 1727.69  11 76  \n2 Solarization of \nPanchayat Samiti \nOffices \n189 2595  4 55  \n3 Solarization of \nKasturba Gandhi \nBalika Vidyalaya \n29 290  1* 10 \n4 Solarization of \nOdisha Aadarsha \nVidyalaya \n40 800  2* 40 \n5 Solarization of Health \nInstitutions \n70 498  2 4  \n6 Solarization of Mines \nunder Odisha Mining \nCorporation \n12 1000  1 200  \nTOTAL 653 6910.69 21 385 \n \n*  Plants completed. Remaining plants are under implementation. \n  \n\nANNEXURE-II REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B)  of LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 270 FOR 16.12.2021 \n \nEXPENDITURE INCURRED IN SOLAR PLANTS IN ODISHA  AND JAJPUR \nDISTRICT \nSl. \nNo \nName of the Plant State Jajpur \nExpenditure in INR Expenditure in INR \n1 Solarization of Fire Stations  7,36,00,181.10  - \n2 Solarization of Panchayat Samiti \nOffices \n5,78,77,860.00 - \n3 Solarization of Kasturba Gandhi Balika \nVidyalaya \n1,54,27,035.00 11,86,695.00 \n4 Solarization of Odisha Aadarsha \nVidyalaya \n2,13,91,200.00 53,47,800.00 \n5 Solarization of Health Institutions 45,80,457.84 - \n6 Solarization of Mines under Odisha \nMining Corporation \n- - \nTOTAL 17,28,76,733.94 65,34,495.00 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |271", "t": "Monitoring of Coopertive Banks", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 271 \nANSWERED ON 16TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n  \nCONSTRUCTION OF NH – 183A \n  \n271.  SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details and the present status of National Highway (NH)-183A in \nthe State of Kerala;  \n(b) whether the Government has completed acquisition of required land \nfor construction of this NH and if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the details of the number of bypasses required on this NH and those \nconstructed on it; and  \n(d) the time by which this NH is likely to be completed along with \nestimated cost thereof?  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) to (d)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION No. 271 FOR ANSWER ON 16.12.2021 \nASKED BY SHRI ANTO ANTONY  REGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF NH -\n183A IN KERALA. \n  \n(a) to (d) Detailed feasibility & Project report is under preparation. On \ncompletion of the report, decision will be taken for further improvement \nof NH-183A based on traffic density, inter -se priority and availability of \nfunds.      \n  \n       \n  \n***** \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |272", "t": "MoU with Fiji", "head": "O.I.H \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 272 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 16, 2021 \n \nPUCCA HOUSES IN URBAN AREAS \n \nNO. 272. SHRI KANAKMAL KATARA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a)  the details of the steps taken to provide pucca hou ses to all in \nurban areas of Rajasthan; \n(b)  the number of urban houses sanctioned in Banswara a nd \nDungarpur districts along with the details of the n umber of \nhouses still required, \n(c)  whether the quality and other parameters of houses are being \nchecked from time to time; and  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n...2/ \n  \n\n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QU ESTION \nNO. 272 (12 TH POSITION) FOR 16.12.2021 REGARDING ‘PUCCA HOUSES IN  \nURBAN AREAS’ \n \n(a)  : Land and Colonization are State Subjects. Schemes  on housing are \nimplemented by States/ UTs. However, Ministry of Ho using and Urban \nAffairs under the vision of ‘Housing for All’ is su pplementing the efforts \nof States/ UTs by providing central assistance unde r Pradhan Mantri \nAwas Yojana- Urban (PMAY-U) to construct houses for  all eligible \nfamilies/ beneficiaries across the country includin g Rajasthan. Details \nof the scheme is available at https://pmay-\nurban.gov.in/uploads/guidelines/60180813309f2-\nUpdated%20guidelines%20of%20PMAY-U.pdf .  \n(b)  : The number of houses sanctioned under PMAY-U in B answara and \nDungarpur districts is 961 and 627 respectively. No  fresh demand is \npending from these districts.  \n(c)  & (d): Yes, Sir. As per the PMAY-U scheme guideline s, States/UTs \nengage Third Party Quality Monitoring Agencies (TPQ MA) to ensure \nquality of construction under various components of  the Mission to \nvisit the project site from time to time and to adv ise State/ UT and \nUrban Local Bodies on quality related issues. On th e basis of quality \nassurance report by such agencies and also reports of their own \ntechnical staff, States and ULBs are mandated to ta ke both preventive \nand curative measures to ensure standard quality ho uses and related \ninfrastructure. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |273", "t": "Assistance to Farmers in Odisha", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 273 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 16, 2021 \nTARGETS UNDER PMAY-U \nNO. 273. SHRI MANOJ KOTAK: \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be p leased to \nstate:  \n(a) whether the Government has announced any target  regarding \nhousing by the year 2022 under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana   \n(PMAY-U) in the country; \n(b) if so, whether the targeted beneficiaries are m ainly from EWS \ncategories and if so, the criteria for their selection; \n(c) the State/UT-wise details of houses sanctioned for the \nbeneficiaries so far and category-wise in Maharasht ra \nespecially in Mumbai; and \n(d) the total funds sanctioned and released under t he Yojana so \nfar, State/UT-wise? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.273 \nto be answered on December 16, 2021 regarding “Targ ets Under \nPMAY-U”. \n(a)&(b) In pursuance of the Government’s vision of “Housing for All” \nby 2022, the Union Government, through Ministry of Housing and \nUrban Affairs (MoHUA), is implementing Pradhan Mant ri Awas \nYojana-Urban (PMAY-U) since 25.06.2015 for giving C entral \nassistance to States/ Union Territories (UTs) for p roviding all-\nweather  “pucca” houses to all eligible urban house holds, especially \nto Economically Weaker Section (EWS) families/house holds having \nannual income up to B 3.00 lakh. The identification of beneficiaries \nunder PMAY-U is done by respective State/ UT Govern ments as per \neligibility under scheme guidelines.  \nBesides, under Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS) vertical \nof the scheme, interest subsidy on housing loan is available to  \nEWS/Low Income Group (LIG) households. The benefit of interest \nsubsidy was  extended to Middle Income Group (MIG) households \nfrom 01.01.2017 to 31.03.2021. \n Under PMAY-U, there are no year-wise fixed targets . The \nhouses under the scheme are sanctioned based on the  project \nproposals received from respective State/ UT Govern ments as per \ntheir assessed demand. So far, around 114 lakh hous es have been \nsanctioned against assessed demand of 112 lakh hous es, of \nwhicharound 90 lakh have been grounded for construc tion and \nnearly 53 lakh have been completed. \n(c)&(d) Under the scheme, out of around 114 lakh sa nctioned \nhouses pan India, 13,52,471 houses have been sancti oned for the \nState of Maharashtra, which includes 10,07,263 for EWS, 2,16,882 \nfor LIG and 1,28,326 for MIG. In Mumbai city 2,17,4 33  houses have \nbeen sanctioned of which 2,06,106, 3,458, and 7,869  are for EWS, \nLIG and MIG categories, respectively. The State/ UT  wise details of \nhouses sanctioned as well as amount sanctioned and released for \nthe beneficiaries is annexed. \n***** \n\n \nAnnexure referred in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Q.No.273 for 16-12-2021 \n \nStates/UTs wise details of houses sanctioned alongwith central assistance sanctioned & \nreleased, as on 06.12.2021, under PMAY-U \n \nSr.No. \n \nName of the \nState/ UT \nNo of Houses \nSanctioned \nCentral Assistance (B Cr.) \nSanctioned Released \n1 \nStates \nAndhraPradesh 20,40,541  30,995.85  10,168.41 \n2 Bihar 3,64,086  5,690.62  2,469.36 \n3 Chhattisgarh 2,99,390  4,629.79  2,732.01 \n4 Goa 4,156  94.71  94.17 \n5 Gujarat 8,56,982  16,300.63  12,161.13 \n6 Haryana 1,55,696  2,719.86  1,214.51 \n7 HimachalPradesh 12,682  225.73  135.97 \n8 Jharkhand 2,34,778  3,595.15  2,461.86 \n9 Karnataka 6,93,577  11,304.59  5,247.75 \n10 Kerala 1,39,848  2,295.94  1,514.37 \n11 MadhyaPradesh 8,65,129  13,975.40  10,088.63 \n12 Maharashtra 13,52,471  22,734.42  11,386.65 \n13 Odisha 2,05,999  3,227.24  1,634.23 \n14 Punjab 1,10,883  1,865.08  1,115.45 \n15 Rajasthan 2,19,535  3,997.88  2,466.25 \n16 TamilNadu 7,19,853  11,486.52  7,632.90 \n17 Telangana 2,33,108  4,057.14  2,827.41 \n18 UttarPradesh 17,67,146  27,535.58  17,109.73 \n19 Uttarakhand 52,486  964.31  575.36 \n20 WestBengal 5,56,646  8,835.51  5,282.30 \nSub-total(States):- 1,08,84,992  1,76,531.95  98,318.45 \n21 \nNorth East States \nArunachalPradesh 9,135  192.64  149.06 \n22 Assam 1,68,261  2,544.92  982.71 \n23 Manipur 56,095  841.88  338.13 \n24 Meghalaya 5,333  85.43  37.57 \n25 Mizoram 39,872  608.27  189.90 \n26 Nagaland 32,331  510.94  306.91 \n27 Sikkim 637  9.83  4.97 \n28 Tripura 92,128  1,477.20  1,029.58 \nSub-total(N.E.States):- 4,03,792  6,271.11  3,038.83 \n29 \nUnionTerritories \nA&NIsland(UT) 602  9.21  1.93 \n30 Chandigarh(UT) 1,582  35.34  35.34 \n31 UTofDNH&DD 8,174  164.53  142.59 \n32 Delhi(NCR) 25,949  588.20  588.20 \n33 J&K (UT) 48,709  747.01  325.93 \n34 Ladakh (UT) 1,373  30.61  21.72 \n35 Lakshadweep(UT) - - - \n36 Puducherry(UT) 14,942  237.92  171.98 \nSub- total(UT):- 1,01,331  1,812.82  1,287.69 \nGrandTotal:- 1.14Crore  1.85LakhCr.  1.03LakhCr. \n. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |274", "t": "ODOP in Kerala", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \n  DEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *274 \nANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 \n \nRESTORATION OF WATER BODIES \n \n*274.  SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI  \nSHRI JAYANT SINHA  \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether any projects have been carried out or a re proposed to be carried out under Renovation, \nRejuvenation and Restoration (RRR) of water bodies in the country including NCR region and Jharkhand \nand if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) the details of funds allocated and utilized und er RRR of water bodies scheme in the country includ ing \nNCR region and Jharkhand;  \n(c) the details of projects on cleaning of traditio nal water bodies in the country including NCR regio n and \nJharkhand completed and expenses incurred for the same from 2016, year-wise; and  \n(d) the steps taken by the Government for preventio n of encroachment of water bodies across the countr y \nincluding NCR region and Jharkhand?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI   \n \n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT) \n \n(a) to (d)   A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n***** \n  \n  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED QUESTION \nNO.*274 TO BE ANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 IN LOK SABHA R EGARDING “RESTORATION \nOF WATER BODIES” ASKED BY SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI AND S HRI JAYANT SINHA, \nHON’BLE M.P., LOK SABHA.  \n  \n(a) & (b)   A scheme titled Repair, Renovation and Restoration (RRR) of Water Bodies is being \nimplemented under Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Y ojana - Har Khet Ko Pani (PMKSY – HKKP). \nObjectives of the scheme include expanding cultivab le area under assured irrigation by improvement and  \nrestoration of water bodies thereby increasing the tank storage capacity and revival of lost irrigatio n \npotential, improving water use efficiency, ground w ater recharge, increased availability of drinking w ater, \nimprovement of catchment of tank commands, and development of tourism & cultural activities, etc. \n \nFrom XIIth Plan onwards, 2,218 water bodies with an  estimated cost of about Rs. 1,910 crore have \nbeen included under RRR of water bodies scheme from  various States. Total expenditure reported on thes e \nprojects till March, 2021 is Rs. 963.82 crore, for which central assistance of Rs.469.68 crore has bee n \nreleased during this period. Out of these 2,218 wat er bodies, works in 1,591 water bodies have been \ncompleted till March, 2021. \n \nHowever,  no proposal for projects pertaining to NC R or Jharkhand have been received for \ninclusion under the scheme. \n \n(c)   Water being a State subject, it is for the State Go vernments concerned to take up schemes related to \nwater bodies, including those for cleaning of tradi tional water bodies. Role of Government of India is  \nlimited to providing technical support and, in some  cases, partial financial assistance under the exis ting \nschemes. In order to supplement the efforts of Stat e Governments in this regard, Government of India h as \ntaken up a number of measures. \n \nUnder RRR of water bodies scheme under Har Khet Ko Pani, work in some of the projects also \nincludes cleaning of traditional water bodies. For the period April 2016 to March, 2021, a 924 project s \nhave been included for repair, renovation and resto ration of water bodies, under the scheme. Rs. 279.1 4 \ncrore has been spent on these projects during April  2016 to March, 2021, against which central assista nce \nof Rs.178.1 crore has been released during this period. Out of these, work for RRR of 428 water bodies has \nbeen completed during April, 2016 to March, 2021. H owever, none of these projects pertains to NCR or \nJharkhand. \n \nRejuvenation of water bodies, including cleaning of  traditional water bodies, is also a component \nunder water supply sector of Atal Mission for Rejuv enation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) scheme \nunder Ministry of Housing & Urban Affairs. Such pro jects with total estimated cost of Rs. 1,878.19 cro re \nare ongoing/completed and 106 water bodies have bee n rejuvenated under this scheme. While there is no \nproject under AMRUT from NCR, details of projects from Jharkhand under this scheme, are as below: \n \n\n  \n Sr. \nNo.  \nName of City  Project Title  \nCost (Rs. in \ncrore)  \nMile Stone  \nNo of Water \nBodies \nRejuvenated  \n1 Ranchi  Ranchi Water Supply (Ph-I)  266.15  Ongoing  4 \n2 Adityapur  \nAdityapur Water Supply \nProject \n \n326.55  Ongoing  3 \n3 Chas  Chas Water Supply Project  129.29  Ongoing  3 \n4 Giridih  Giridih Water Supply Project  36.32  Completed  3 \n5 Dhanbad  Dhanbad Water Supply (Ph-I)  159.31  Ongoing  7 \n6 Hazaribag  \nHazaribag Water Supply \nProject \n \n416.56  Ongoing  4 \n             \n (d)    Water being a State subject, it is for the State Go vernments concerned to take up programmes and \nschemes for prevention of encroachment of its water  bodies. However, in order to supplement the \nefforts of State Governments, Government of "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |275", "t": "Panchayati Raj Instituions", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO- 275 \nANSWERED ON- 30/11/2021 \n \nPANCHAYATI RAJ INSTITUTIONS \n \n275. SHRI PATEL HASMUKHBHAI SOMABHAI: \n        \n Will the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state:- \n \n(a)  whether any mechanism has been developed within the Panchayati Raj Institutions to \nprepare district plans and to monitor the works executed by Gram Panchayats;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  whether some Panchayats in the country have expressed th eir inability to utilize funds \nearmarked for them due to non-availability of district plans;  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(e)  whether the Government has issued any instructions to the Panchayats in this regard; \nand  \n(f)  if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n \n(a) Yes Sir. \n \n(b) The devolution of funds to all the three tiers of Panchayats including District \nPanchayats under the XV Finance Commission (XVFC) has necessitated a need to prepare \nDistrict Panchayat Development plans which is a mandatory condition under XVFC Grants. In \nthis context, Ministry of Panchayati Raj has developed a Framework for Preparation of Block  \nPanchayat Development Plan (BPDP) and District Panchayat Development Plans (DPDP) on \n28.10.2020 to Support States in preparation of the Block and District Development Plans for \nFY 2020 -21 onwards and shared with states. Further, handholding support and ca pacity \nbuilding & training has been provided through National Institute for Rural Development & \nPanchayati Raj (NIRD&PR) to stakeholders in cascade mode in preparation of Developments \n\nPlans at the Block and District level. Training has been imparted to 327  State Level Master \nTrainers from 34 States/ UTs for implementation of BPDP & DPDP in coordination with \nNIRD&PR. For preparation and monitoring of BPDP & DPDP, 27 States/UTs have set up their \nDistrict Level and 15 States have set their Block Level Control Room and a total of 540 District \nlevel Control Rooms have been set up so far. To provide instant guidance to Planning Teams \noperating at District Level, all the States/ UTs have been advised to set -up a District level \nControl Room cum Project Management Un it (PMU) that serves as a mechanism for proper \npreparation and implementation of DPDPs. Panchayat being State subject, monitoring of the \nworks being executed by Gram Panchayats is primarily responsibility of State Governments.  \n \nTo facilitate States to mon itor the progress of activities being undertaken at Gram \nPanchayat level, the Ministry has launched e-Gram SWARAJ (https://egramswaraj.gov.in/), a \nunified tool for effective monitoring and evaluation of works taken up in the Panchayats on \n24th April, 2020.  The application improves reporting and tracking of Panchayat activities, \nproviding a single interface for capturing Panchayat information. The (e -Gram SWARAJ) \napplication strengthens and decentralizes planning process so that the development funds \nconsumed by the Plans result in effective outcomes. The application focuses on Work Based \nAccounting, tracking the expenditure incurred for each of the activities proposed under the \nPanchayat Development Plan. \n \n(c) No Sir. \n \n(d) Does not arise in view of above,  \n \n(e) Yes Sir. \n \n(f) The States have been advised to issue suitable instructions to District Panchayats/ \nIntermediate Panchayats/ equivalent Traditional Bodies to prepare Plans and upload them on \neGramSwaraj portal after due approvals so that the expenditure from the XV FC funds are \nincurred by them as per those plans only. \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |276", "t": "Complaints regarding Kendriya Bhandar", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \n  DEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *276 \nANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 \n \nKALESHWARAM IRRIGATION PROJECT \n \n*276.  SHRI UTTAM KUMAR REDDY NALAMADA  \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Union Government has approved the K aleshwaram Irrigation Project (KIP) in the State of  \nTelangana and if so, the details of tendering process and physical progress thereof;  \n(b) whether the KIP has created any new ayacut and if so, the details of additional irrigation water t o be \nsupplied by the project, the total area of addition al land irrigated, the amount of water envisaged to  be \nlifted in the main and additional KIP, location and  district-wise along with the total cost incurred o n the \nproject so far;  \n(c) the details of funding by the Union Government and its entities such as Power Finance Corporation,  \nRural Electrification Corporation and nationalised banks to the above project;  \n(d) whether the Union Government has assessed the c ost-benefit ratio of the Kaleshwaram main and \nadditional projects and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) the details of agencies entrusted with the execution of main and additional Kaleshwaram projects?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI   \n \n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT) \n \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n*****  \n  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e)  OF STARRED QUESTION \nNo.*276 TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 16.12.2021 R EGARDING “KALESHWARAM \nIRRIGATION PROJECT” ASKED BY UTTAM KUMAR REDDY NALAMADA.  \n \n(a)  Kaleshwaram Irrigation Project (KIP) has been accep ted by the Advisory Committee on Irrigation, \nFlood Control and Multipurpose Projects of Ministry  of Jal Shakti, in June, 2018. The project is being  \nexecuted by the State Government of Telangana from its own resources. As informed by the State \nGovernment, tenders for the project were invited on  e-procurement platform based on lump-sum contract \nsystem.  \n \nFurther, as informed by the State Government, physi cal progress achieved on KIP till 31.10.2021 is \n83.7%.  \n \n(b) As informed by the State Government, total command area proposed to be irrigated under KIP is \n18,25,700 acres. Additionally, stabilization of an area of 18,82,970 acre of land is envisaged. The St ate \nGovernment has further informed that total amount o f water envisaged to be lifted and supplied in the \nproject is 240 thousand million cubic feet (TMC).  \n \nNew areas in varying proportion of thirteen distric ts of the State viz., Karimnagar, Rajanna Sircilla,  \nSiddipet, Medak, Yadadri-Bhongiri, Nalgonda, Sangar eddy, Nizamabad, Jagityal, Kamareddy, Nirmal, \nMedchal, Peddapalli etc., are proposed to be covered under irrigation by the project.  \n \nThe total cost incurred on KIP so far is reported to be Rs. 80,321.57 crore.  \n \n(c)  As per information provided by the State Government , details of funding provided by various agencies \nto the project, are given below:  \n(Rs. in crore)  \nSl. No  Name of the bank/FIs  \nAmount \nSanctioned  Amount Released  \n1 Union Bank of India consortium  7,400.00  7,400.00  \n2 Punjab National Bank Consortium  11,400.00  11,355.20  \n3 Bank of Baroda  2,150.00  2,150.00  \n4 Power Finance Corporation  26,351.96  23,584.72  \n5 Rural Electrification Corporation Ltd.  30,536.08  9,633.65  \n6 NABARD  8,225.97  5,415.94  \nTOTAL  86,064.01  59,539.51  \n  \n(d)  The estimated cost of Kaleshwaram project has been finalized for Rs.80,190.46 crore (price level 2015-\n16) by Advisory Committee on Irrigation, Flood Cont rol and Multipurpose Projects (Advisory Committee) \nof Ministry of Jal Shakti, in June, 2018, at which the Benefit Cost Ratio worked out to be 1.51. Howev er, \nthe proposal for subsequent additional components o f the project have not been submitted by the State \nGovernment for consideration of the Advisory Committee.  \n \n(e)  A list of agencies entrusted with the works of the project is enclosed as Annexure . \n*****  \n\nANNEXURE  \n \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (e) OF STA RRED Q. NO. *276 TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 16.12.2021 REGARDING “KALESHWARAM IRRIGATION \nPROJECT”. \n List of agencies entrusted with the works of the project \n \nPackage No.  Name of the Contractor  \n2TMC PER DAY  \nMedigadda Barrage  M/s. L&T – PES(JV)  \nAnnaram Barrage  M/s. AFCONS – VIJETHA- PES(JV)  \nSundilla Barrage  M/s. NAVAYUGA – GMW (JV)  \nMedigadda - Annaram Lift System  M/s.MEIL – NCC(JV)  \nAnnaram - Sundilla Lift System  M/s. MEIL  \nSundilla - SYP Lift System  M/s. MEIL  \n6 M/s.NAVAYUGA-PATEL-BHEL(Consortium)  \n7 M/s.MAYTAS-MEIL-ABB-AAG(JV)  \nMedaram reservoir  M/s. Sri Raja Rajeswari Constructions (I) Pvt. Ltd. \n8 M/s.MEIL-SEW-MAYTAS-BHEL(Consortium)  \n9 M/s.IVRCL-BATPASCO-WPIL-MHI(JV)  \n9 – 60(c)-1 M/s MRKR Constructions & Industries Pvt. Ltd  \n9 – 60(c)-2 M/s MRKR Constructions & Industries Pvt. Ltd  \n9 – 60(c)-3"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |277", "t": "MoU with Flipkart under National Rural Livelihood Mission", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 277 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nMOU WITH FLIPKART UNDER NATIONAL RURAL LIVELIHOOD MISSION \n \n277.  SHRI P.V. MIDHUN REDDY: \nSHRI TALARI RANGAIAH: \nSHRI N. REDDEPPA: \nDR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI: \nSHRI ADALA PRABHAKARA REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has signed a  Memorandum of Understanding(MoU) with \nFlipkart for partnership under the National Rural Livelihood Mission; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  whether the Government has marketed the  products earlier through State owned \nonline E-commerce Platform as well as other commercial E-commerce Platforms; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a) Yes Sir. \n(b) A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) is entered on November 2 nd, 2021 between \nMinistry of Rural Development and Flipkart Internet Pvt. Ltd. to allow the Self Help \nGroups (SHGs) producers including the artisans, weavers and craftsmen to access \nnational markets through the Flipkart Samarth programme. \n            The key features of MoU are as follows: \n \ni. SHG members and Clusters (geographical grouping of SHGs) will be provided   \ntraining  support for on-boarding products. \nii. Waiver of all commission charges for selling on the platform for a period of 6 \nmonths \niii. Cataloguing support for a maximum of 100 products per seller \niv. Other benefits like support for warehousing and account management etc. \n      (c) Yes Sir.   \n  \n(d) The Ministry in collaboration with Government e -Marketplace (GeM) has created \n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������   \n  \nThe States of Assam, Bihar, Ch hattisgarh, Gujarat, Himachal Pradesh, Jharkhand, \nKarnataka, Kerala, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Odisha, Punjab, Rajasthan, \n\nUttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh & West Bengal have supported SHGs in registering on the \nGeM portal. \n  \nJharkhand has supported SHGs to re gister on Amazon and Flipkart while Kerala and \nMaharashtra have supported SHGs to register on Amazon. \n  \nThe four States of Assam, Bihar, Kerala and Madhya Pradesh have developed e -\ncommerce platforms to support SHGs; the details are provided below \n  \n \n***** \n \n \nS.No State Name of Site \n1 Assam Asomi \n2 Bihar Jeevika Shop \n3 Kerala Kudumbashree Bazaar \n4 Madhya Pradesh Madhya Pradesh Aajeevika Mart "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |278", "t": "Technical-organizational Restructure in Fisheries", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 278  \nANSWERED ON 16TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n  \nNH PROJECTS IN KARNATAKA \n  \n*278.   G.M. SIDDESHWAR: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of new National Highways (NHs) sanctioned for \nconstruction in the State of Karnataka during the last three years;  \n(b) whether the Government has received any proposal from the State \nGovernment during the said period for construction of new NHs;  \n(c) if so, the action taken thereon; and \n(d) the funds allocated, released and utilised for development and \nconstruction of NHs in Karnataka during the said period, year-wise? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI)  \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 278 FOR ANSWER ON 16 .12.2021 \nASKED BY SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR  REGARDING NH PROJECTS IN \nKARNATAKA. \n \n(a) to (d) Ministry of Transport & Highways had received 6 proposals \nfor declaration of new National Highways during the last 3 years from \nGovernment of Karnataka. Of these Ministry had declared 3 roads as \nnew National Highways (NHs), namely, NH-766E, NH-766EE and NE7. \nMinistry has taken up 5 projects in these newly declared NHs i.e., NH-\n766E, NH -766EE & NE7 under Bharatmala Pariyojana & Port \nConnectivity program. The details of funds allocated and utilized for \ndevelopment / construction of NHs in the State of Karnataka during \nthe said period, year-wise are as below; \nRs in Crore \nYear Allocation Expenditure \n2018-19 5340.67 5340.67 \n2019-20 9340.20 9340.20 \n2020-21 5797.05 5797.05 \n  \n  \n**** \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |279", "t": "PMGSY-III in Kerala and Tamil Nadu", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \n  DEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*279 \nANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 \n \nDATABASE ON WATER \n \n†*279.         SHRI NAYAB SINGH  \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has devised any special scheme for comprehensive database on water in \npublic sector and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) whether the Government has made an assessment o f the impact of climate change on water resources \nand if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the plan of the Government for focussing attention on the sensitive including over exploited areas; and  \n(d) the details of the achievements made so far und er ‘Catch the Rain’ initiative, State-wise along with the \nname of the State with the best performance thereunder?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI   \n \n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n******  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED QUESTION NO. \n†*279  TO BE ANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 IN LOK SABHA REGARDING  “DATABASE ON \nWATER” ASKED BY SHRI NAYAB SINGH.  \n  \n(a)   The Central Government has created National W ater Informatics Centre (NWIC), a subordinate \norganization under this Department in March, 2018 to act as a central repository with a mandate to  co llect, \ncollate, maintain and disseminate all information r elated to water resources in the country. NWIC \nmaintains a web platform with web-link https://indiawris.gov.in  in public domain which hosts the \ncomprehensive data related to water sector.  \n  \n (b) Ministry of Earth Sciences has publised a repo rt in 2020 “Assessment of Climate Change over the \nIndian Region,” which includes the impact on water resources. In addition, a number of research projec ts \non the impact of climate change on water resources have been taken up through IITs, NITs etc. \n  \n(c)      Water is a State subject but the Central G overnment supports the States with technical and fi nancial \nsupport. The Government  has taken a number of impo rtant measures for conservation, management of \nground water and effective implementation of rain water harvesting in the country including over-exploited \nareas, which can be seen at \nURL:http://jalshaktidowr.gov.in/sites/default/files/Steps_to_control_water_depletion_Feb2021.pdf. Some  \nof the important initiatives in this regard are also given at Annexure I.  \n \nIn addition, a number of States have done notable w ork in the field of water \nconservation/harvesting such as ‘Mukhyamantri Jal S wavlamban Abhiyan’ in Rajasthan, ‘Jalyukt Shibar’ \nin Maharashtra, ‘Sujalam Sufalam Abhiyan’ in Gujarat, ‘Mission Kakatiya’ in Telangana, Neeru Chettu’ in \nAndhra Pradesh, Jal Jeevan Hariyali in Bihar, ‘Jal Hi Jeevan’ in Haryana, and Kudimaramath scheme in \nTamil Nadu. \n   \n(d)  Ministry of Jal Shakti has taken up the “Jal Shakti  Abhiyan: Catch the Rain” (JSA:CTR) with the \ntheme “Catch the Rain - Where it Falls When it Falls” to cover all the blocks of all districts (rural as well as \nurban areas) across the country during 22nd March 2 021 to 30th November 2021. The campaign was \nlaunched by the Hon’ble Prime Minister on 22 March 2021. The details of State-wise achievements of the  \nStates is given in Annexure II.  \n  \n \n***** \n \n \n\nANNEXURE-I  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF STARRE D QUESTION NO.†*279  TO \nBE ANSWERED ON 16.12.2021 IN LOK SABHA REGARDING “DATABASE ON WATER”. \n  \nImportant initiatives on management of groundwater resources  \n  \nGovernment of India launched Jal Shakti Abhiyan (JS A) in 2019, a time bound campaign with a mission \nmode approach intended to improve water availabilit y including ground water conditions in the water \nstressed blocks of 256 districts in India. In this regard, teams of officers from Central Government a long-\nwith technical officers from Ministry of Jal Shakti were deputed to visit water stressed districts and to work \nin close collaboration with district level officials to undertake suitable interventions.  \n  \nIn addition, Ministry of Jal Shakti has taken up th e “Jal Shakti Abhiyan: Catch the Rain” (JSA:CTR) wi th \nthe theme “Catch the Rain - Where it Falls When it Falls” to cover all the blocks of all districts (ru ral as \nwell as urban areas) across the country during 22nd  March 2021 to 30th November 2021. The campaign \nwas launched by the Hon’ble Prime Minister on 22 March 2021.  \n  \nMinistry of Jal Shakti, Department of Water Resourc es, RD & GR (DoWR, RD & GR) is implementing \nAtal Bhujal Yojana (Atal Jal), a Rs.6,000 crore Cen tral Sector Scheme, for sustainable management of \nground water resources with community participation . Atal Jal is being implemented in 81 water stresse d \ndistricts and 8,774 Gram Panchayats of seven States  viz. Gujarat, Haryana, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, \nMaharashtra, Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh.  \n  \nCentral Ground Water Boar"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |28", "t": "Changes in Forest Conservation Act", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *28 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021/ AGRAHAYANA 9, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nDISASTER RELIEF THROUGH NDRF AND SDRF \n \n*28.      SHRI OMPRAKASH BHUPALSINH ALIAS  \n    PAWAN RAJENIMBALKAR: \n    SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether National Disaster Response Fund  (NDRF) and State Disaster \nResponse Fund (SDRF) have  been set up jointly by the Union Government/State \nGovernments to provide relief to the persons affected by  natural disasters in \nStates; \n \n(b) if so, the present status thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Union Government had  fixed the  rates for State Disaster \nResponse Fund (SDRF) during the period from the year 2015 to 2020; \n \n(d) if so, the steps being taken by the Government to increase the said rate; \n \n(e) whether any proposal relating to increase in the  said rate has been received \nfrom the State Government  of Maharashtra and if so, the action take n by the  \nGovernment thereon; and \n \n(f) the details of funds released by the Union  Government in this regard during \nthe last five years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (f): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. \n*28 DATED 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \n \n(a) and (b):  Yes sir.  National Disaster Response Fund (NDRF) has been \nconstituted by the Central Government as per  the provision of Section 46(1) of \nthe Disaster Management (DM) Act, 2005, for meeting any threatening disaster \nmanagement situation or disaster.  Similarly, as per the provision of Section \n48(1)(a) of the Act, all the State Governments have constituted State D isaster \nResponse Fund (SDRF) in their respective State.  \n Funds under SDRF and NDRF are allocated by the Central Government, \nbased on the recommendations of the successive Finance Commissions.  Funds \nfor NDRF are fully contributed by the Central Government , whereas, the funds in \nSDRF are contributed by the Central Government and State Governments in the \nratio of 75:25 for general category States and 90:10 for North -Eastern and \nHimalayan States.  \nThe release of funds from SDRF/NDRF and expenditure therefrom are \ngoverned by the ‘Guidelines on constitution and administration of SDRF/ NDRF’ \nand items and norms issued by Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA), from time to \ntime.     \n(c)  to (f):  Yes sir.  The revision of guidelines and items and norms are done \nbased on the recommendations of the successive Finance Commissions as per \nthe established procedure.  After the recommendations of the 15 th Finance \nCommission, the process  for the revision of item and nor ms for the expenditure  \nfrom NDRF/ SDRF during the award period of the 15 th Finance Commission i.e. \n\nupto 2026 has been initiated by constituting a Committee, consisting of \nmembers from the Central Ministries and State Governments, inclu ding the State \nof Mah arashtra. The Committee is in the process of finalizing its \nrecommendations by taking into consideration the suggestions of all the State \nGovernments and other stakeholders, including the suggestions received from \nthe Government of Maharashtra.   \n The details of funds released to Government of Maharashtra under SDRF/ \nNDRF during last five years are as under:- \n(Rs. in crore) \nYear SDRF Allocation Central \nShare \nreleased \nNDRF \nCentral \nShare \nState \nShare \nTotal \n2016-17 1167.75 389.25 1557.00 583.875 2224.78 \n2017-18 1226.25 408.75 1635.00 1810.125 - \n2018-19 1287.75 429.25 1717.00 1287.75 2088.59 \n2019-20 1352.25 450.75 1803.00 1352.25 5189.40 \n2020-21 3222.00 1074.00 4296.00* 3222.00 420.12 \n*  It also includes 20% amount earmarked for State Disaster Mitigation Fund \n(SDMF). \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |280", "t": "Blue Revolution in Andhra Pradesh", "head": "GOVERNMENT \nOF \nINDIA\n \nMINISTRY \nOF \nMICRO,\n \nSMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION No.\n \n*280\n \nTO BE \nANSWERED \nON\n \n16.12.2021\n \n \nMSME\ns\n \nIN WEST BENGAL\n \n \n*280.\n \n \nSHRI RAJU BISTA:\n \n \n \nWill \nthe \nMinister \nof \nMICRO, SMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES \nbe pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe number of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) functioning in \nWest Bengal as on date;\n \n \n(b)\n \nthe data on the number of MSMEs in Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts;\n \n(c)\n \nthe details of loans sanctioned under the MUDRA Yojana in Darjeeling and \nKalimp\nong districts since the inception of the scheme; and \n \n(d)\n \nthe details of loans disbursed to the MSME sector under Prime Minister Aatma \nNirbhar Bharat Scheme and the number of MSMEs benefitted therefrom in Darjeeling \nand Kalimpong districts?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER\n \nOF \nMICRO, SMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(\nSHRI\n \nNARAYAN RANE\n)\n \n \n(a) to (d): \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION No. 280  FOR ANSWER ON 16.12.2021\n \n(a)& (b)\n:\n \nAs per Udyam Registration Portal, the total number of classified micro, \nsmall and medium enterprises registered in Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts and in \nthe state of West Bengal as on 12.12.2021 is given below:\n \nDistrict/State*\n \nMicro\n \nSmall\n \nMedium\n \nTotal\n \nDARJEELING\n \n5,258\n \n625\n \n54\n \n5,937\n \nKALIMPONG\n \n354\n \n12\n \n0\n \n366\n \nWEST BENGAL\n \n1,53,190\n \n13,430\n \n1,604\n \n168,224\n \n    \n*From 01.07.2020 to 12.12.2021\n \n \n(c)\n:\n \nThe details\n \nof loan sanctioned under Mudra Yojana in Darjeeling and \nKalimpong districts are given below:\n \n \nDistrict\n \nNumber of Accounts \nSanctioned\n \nSanctioned Amount\n \n(Rs in Crore)\n \nDARJEELING*\n \n8,57,840\n \n4,220.90\n \nKALIMPONG*\n \n8,377\n \n55.58\n \n*Mudra Portal (District wise data is available since 01.04.2016 till 26.11.2021)\n \n(d)\n:\n \nThe details of loan disbursed in Darjeeling and \nKalimpong districts under \nEmergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS) under Aatma Nirbhar Bharat \nScheme is given below:\n \n \nDistrict\n \nEmergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme\n \nNumber of \nDisbursement\n \nDisbursement \nAmount\n \n(Rs in Crore)\n \nDARJEELING\n \n67,564\n \n378.04\n \nKALIMPONG\n \n1,788\n \n5.38\n \n \nUnder C\nredit Guarantee Scheme for Subordinate Debt (CGSSD), the number\n \nof\n \nguarantees approved and amount of guarantees approved in West Bengal were 25 \nand Rs.2.06 crore respectively as on 03.12.2021.\n \n*\n**\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |281", "t": "Construction of Stadium to Promote Sports", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †281 \nANSWERED ON 30.11.2021 \n \nConstruction of Stadium to Promote Sports \n \n†281. SHRI DULAL CHAND GOSWAMI: \nSHRI CHANDESHWAR PRASAD: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to construct stadiums at \ndistrict/block/panchayat level in the States to promote sports in the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the details of the progress made in \nthis regard so far; and \n \n(c) the details of the number of stadiums constructed so far  at \nblock/panchayat level in the country during the last two years, State -wise \nincluding Katihar, Jehanabad, Gaya and Arwal district of the state of Bihar? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR } \n \n(a) to (c) ‘Sports’ being a State subject, the primary responsibility to \nconstruct stadiums  at district/block/panchayat level  rests with the \nState/Union Territory Governm ents. The Union Government s upplements \ntheir efforts. The stadiums in various parts of the country, including Bihar, \nare under the jurisdiction of respective bodies/departments of State/UT \nGovernments. As such, the information about them is not maintained in this \nMinistry. However, t his Ministry has sanctioned 267 sports infrastructure \nprojects of various categories across the country under the Khelo India \nScheme, which includes 11 projects in Bihar. \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |282", "t": "Agricultural Techniques", "head": "1 \n \nO.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL RESEARCH & EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 282 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \n \nAGRICULTURAL TECHNIQUES \n \n282. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE    \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any scheme is being run by the Government to provide information to \nthe farmers regarding latest agriculture techniques;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the total number of farmers benifitted under said scheme in the  State of Uttar \nPradesh, district-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h    (SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) & (b) The Government has set up a network of Krishi Vigyan Kendras \n(KVKs) in the Country to provide information to the farmers about latest agriculture \ntechniques. The activities of KVKs in clude On -farm testing to identify the location \nspecificity of technology under various farming systems; Frontline demonstration to \nestablish the production potential of improved agricultural technologies on the \nfarmers; fields; Capacity development of fa rmers for knowledge and skill up \ngradation; providing farm advisories using ICT and other media means on varied \nsubjects of interest to famers; and production of quality seeds and planting materials \nfor availability to the farmers. In order to develop aware ness of improved agricultural \ntechnology among the farmers, KVKs take up a large number of extension activities. \n(c) District wise number of farmers benefitted under different activities of KVKs in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh during 2020-21 is given in Annexure-I. \n \n******* \n  \n\n2 \n \nANNEXURE-I \n [Part (c) of Lok Sabha USQ No.282 dated 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021] \n \nDistrict wise number of farmers benefitted under different activities of KVKs in the \nState of Uttar Pradesh during last one year \nName of district Number of farmers benefitted Total \nOFT* FLD** T