����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |324", "t": "Fishers Opinion on Indian Marine Fisheries (IMF) Bill", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *324 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 21ST DECEMBER, 2021/ AGRAHAYANA 30, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nADDITIONAL INFRASTRUCTURE FOR NIA \n \n*324.      SHRI MANICKAM TAGORE B.: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the National Investigation  Agency (NIA) needs \nadditional infrastructure and domain  experts to probe cyber terrorism and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n \n(b) whether it is also a fact that the NIA was given  the mandate to probe cases \nrelated to cyber terrorism two years ago; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) the total number of such cases being investigated by NIA as of now? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n-2- \nL.S.S.Q.NO.*324 FOR 21.12.2021 \n \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK  SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*324 FOR 21st \nDECEMBER, 2021 \n \n \n(a) to (d): National Investigation Agency (NIA) has been constituted under NIA \nAct, 2008 to investigate the cases involving offences specified in the schedule to \nthe Act.  The mandate of the NIA has been expanded by inclusion of more \noffences including Section 66F of Chapter XI of the Information Technology Act, \n2000 to its Schedule through National Investigation Agency (Amendment) Act, \n2019.  The Government has entrusted 2 cases registered under 66F of the \nInformation Technology Act, 2000 to the NIA for investigation.   The Government \nof India has consistently taken steps to enhance capacity of the NIA, including \nmanpower and infrastructure, to ensure that it is able to carry out its mandate \neffectively.   \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |325", "t": "Schemes and Facilities for Persons with Disabilities", "head": "O.I.H\n \nGOVERNME\nNT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.325 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 21\nst\n \nDECEMBER \n,2021\n \n \nPM\n-\nKISAN YOJANA \n \n \n†\n325\n.      \nSHRI RAJ KUMAR CHAHAR\n:\n \n    \nMS. \nDEBASREE CHAUDHURI\n: \n \n \nWill the Minister \n \nof \n \nAgriculture and Farmers Welfare\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n(a)\n \nthe amount of funds disbursed to the farmers since the launch of the Pradhan \nMantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) Yojana\n \ntill date, year\n-\nwise\n;\n \n \n(b)   whether there are any other similar programmes initiated by the States that \ncomplement this programme and if so, the details\n \nthereof;\n \n \n(c)     \nthe\n \nmanner in which the farmers deprived of the benefits of the said scheme are \nproposed to be provided these benefits; and \n \n \n(d)      the time by which the said benefits are likely to be provided?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n      \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (d\n):      A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT  TO BE MADE IN REPLY TO L\nOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.325\n \nRAI\nSED BY\n \nSHRI RAJ KUMAR CHAHAR\n \nAND\n \nMS. DEBASREE CHAUDHURI \n, \nDUE \nFOR REPLY ON 21\n.12.\n2021\n.\n \n \n \n(a):\n \nUnder PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme, as on 8\nth\n \nDecember, 2021, more than 11.61\n \ncrore \nfarmers have been given the financial be\nnefits of approximately Rs. 1.61\n \nlakh crore through \nvarious installments.\n \n \nThe year\n-\nwise details of funds \ndisbursed under PM\n-\nKISAN Sc\nheme since its \ninception till 8\nth\n \nDecember, 2021 is placed below: \n \nS.No.\n \nFinancial Year\n \nAmount disbursed (in Crore Rs.)\n \n1.\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n6,005.48\n \n2.\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n4,91,96.38\n \n3.\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n6,10,91.01\n \n4.\n \n2021\n-\n22 (till 8\nth\n \nDecember, 2021)\n \n45,249.81\n \nGrand Total\n \n1,61,542.68\n \n \n(b):\n \nThe Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) is a Central Sector Scheme, \nbeing implemented since 1\nst\n \nDecember, 2018 with an objective of providing financial \nassistance to landholding farmer families across the country, subject to certain exclusion \ncriteria, so that they can be enabled to take care of expenses related to agriculture and \nallied activities \nas well as domestic needs.  Under the Scheme, an amount of Rs. 6000/\n-\n \nper \nyear is transferred in three 4\n-\nmonthly installments of Rs.2000/\n-\n \ndirectly into the bank \naccounts of the farmers. \n \n \n \nT\nhe beneficiaries of PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme, if they are otherwise \neligible, are not \ndebarred to get benefits of any other Scheme implemented by the Union Government or \nState/UT Governments for the welfare of farmers of the country.\n \n \n \n\n(c) & (d):\n \nThe PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme is a continuous and ongoing Scheme under which the \nrespon\nsibility to identify the beneficiaries and uploading their correct and verified data on \nPM\n-\nKISAN web portal lies with the respective State/UT Governments. The data received on \nPM\n-\nKISAN web portal goes through various level of verification and validation li\nke \nAadhaar/PFMS/Income Tax. Consequent upon such verification, the benefits of the Scheme \nare given to intended beneficiaries through Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) mode directly into \ntheir bank accounts. \n \n \n \nF\nor enrollment under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sam\nman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) \nS\ncheme, the farmer\n \napproach\nes\n \nthe local patwari / revenue o\nfficer / Nodal Officer (PM\n-\nKISAN\n) nominated by the State\n/UT\n \nGovernment. However, the following additional steps \nhave \nalso \nbeen taken by the Government to include more and more \neligible farmers under \nthe Scheme.\n \n(i)\n \nThe States are\n \nadvised to organize awareness campaigns and registration camps to \nbring the eligible beneficiaries into the ambit of the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman \nNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) Scheme.  \n \n(ii)\n \nA special feature, vi\nz\n \n“Farmers Corner” is available in the PM\n-\nKISAN portal, throu\ngh \nwhich the farmers can also exercise\n \ntheir self\n-\nregistration. \n \n(iii)\n \nFarmers can also edit their names in PM\n-\nKisan database as per their Aadhaar \ndatabase/ card through the Farmers Corner in the\n \nportal. \n \n(iv) \n \nFarmers can also know the status of their payment through the Farmers Corner in the \nportal. Village\n-\nwise details of beneficiaries are also available on the Farmers Corner. \n \n(v)\n \nFarmers can approach Village Level Entrepreneur (VLEs) of CSCs \nto get enrolled \nthemselves under PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme. The facilities available at Farmers Corner can \nalso be availed through VLEs of CSC. \n \n(vi)\n \nMobile app has been launched which also provides the facilities available at Farmers \nCorner on PM\n-\nKISAN portal. \n \n***\n**\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |326", "t": "Suicides due to Drug Abuse", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 326 \n  ANSWERED ON 21/12/2021 \n \nEMPLOYMENT UNDER DDU-GKY \n \n*326.  SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the employment under Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushal Yojana (DDU-\nGKY) has fallen following the onset of COVID; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  the reasons for the fall in employment rate; and \n(d)  the efforts being made by the Government to  increase the employment under DDU -\nGKY? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n  \n   \n\n \n \nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *326 \ndue for answer on 21.12.2021 \n  \n(a) to (c)  Due to surge in COVID-19 and subsequent lockdowns, all economic activities were \nimpacted including training and placement under DDU-GKY. The number of candidates trained \nand placed under DDUGKY during last three years and the current year are given below: \nFinancial Year  18-19 Financial Year  19-20  Financial Year  20-21  Financial Year  21-22 \ntill Nov'21  \nTrained Placed Trained Placed Trained Placed Trained Placed \n241509 137251 247177 150214 38289 49563 23186 22067 \n  \n(d)  Under DDU-GKY various awareness campaigns, job fairs and meetings of Chief Executive \nOfficers of Companies/Employers have been undertaken by States and UTs for improvement in \nplacement of trained candidates.  \n  \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |327", "t": "Shifting/Jhum Cultivation", "head": "Page 1 of 4 \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *327 \nANSWERED ON 21.12.2021 \n \nFit India Cyclothon \n \n*327. SHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL: \nDR. HEENA GAVIT: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the programmes being undertaken  by the Government for \nidentifying the talents amongst  youth in rural areas of various States and \nUTs particularly in Maharashtra; \n \n(b) the details of the number of beneficiaries  under these programmes \nduring the last five years, State/UT-wise; \n \n(c) the details and the objectives of the ‘Fit India Cyclothon’; \n \n(d) whether the Government has constituted any  Committee/team to assess \nthe condition of all the stadiums in the country; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR } \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n\nPage 2 of 4 \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *327 ANSWERED ON 21.12.2021 REGARDING “FIT \nINDIA CYCLOTHON” ASKED BY SHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL  AND \nDR. HEENA GAVIT, HON’BLE MEMBERS OF LOK SABHA \n \n(a) and (b) The Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports implements the following \nschemes for the development of sports in the country, including for the \nyouth in rural areas of Maharashtra: \n \n(i) Khelo India Scheme; (ii) Assistance to National Sports Federations; (iii) \nSpecial Awards to Winners in International Sports Events and their \nCoaches; (iv) National Spor ts A wards; (v) Pension to Meritorious \nSportspersons; (vi) Pandit Deendayal Upadhyay National Sports Welfare \nFund; (vii) National Sports Development Fund; and (viii) Running Sports \nTraining Centres through Sports Authority of India (SAI). \n \nDetails of the ab ove schemes are available in the public domain on the \nwebsites of this Ministry and SAI. \n \nState/UT-wise details  of number of athletes supported under  Khelo India \nScheme of this Ministry  and Sports Promotional Schemes of SAI and are at \nAnnexure I and II, respectively.  \n \n(c) The Fit India Movement was launched on 29th August, 2019 by the \nHon’ble Prime Minister with a view to make fitness an integral part of our \ndaily lives. Since its inception, this Ministry  has been actively spreading \nawareness about fitness  through various campaigns which , inter-alia, \ninclude a campaign, namely, the Fit India Cyclothon , to create awareness \non fitness through cycling. Fit India Cyclothon can be organised by any \nGovernment or private organisation, school , college , university, individual, \ninterested groups, residential associations, communities in villages, towns, \nworkplaces, etc. \n \n(d) and (e) ‘Sports’ being a State subject, the responsibility for promotion \nand development of sports rests primarily with the respective  State/Union \nTerritory Governments. Central Government only supplements the efforts of \nthe State/UT Governments under its various schemes.  The stadiums under \nthe control of this Ministry have dedicated administrators and the available \nfacilities as well as the  maintenance thereof are reviewed /assessed \nregularly with the service providers and other stakeholders. \n\nPage 3 of 4 \nANNEXURES REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. * 327 ANSWERED ON 21.12.2021 REGARDING “FIT \nINDIA CYCLOTHON” ASKED BY SHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL  AND \nDR. HEENA GAVIT, HON’BLE MEMBERS OF LOK SABHA \n \nANNEXURE – I \n \nState/UT-wise details of athletes supported under the Khelo India Scheme \n \nS. No. State/UT 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 Total \n1 Andaman & Nicobar 11 1 0 12 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 28 25 3 56 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 8 3 0 11 \n4 Assam 34 10 1 45 \n5 Bihar 7 2 4 13 \n6 Chandigarh 29 15 2 46 \n7 Chhattisgarh 22 8 0 30 \n8 Daman & Diu 1 3 0 4 \n9 Delhi 162 73 3 238 \n10 Goa 14 3 1 18 \n11 Gujarat 58 41 1 100 \n12 Haryana 266 142 9 417 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 11 14 0 25 \n14 Jammu & Kashmir 10 8 1 19 \n15 Jharkhand 22 5 5 32 \n16 Karnataka 101 36 5 142 \n17 Kerala 76 39 9 124 \n18 Ladakh 1 1 0 2 \n19 Madhya Pradesh 46 39 7 92 \n20 Maharashtra 244 147 27 418 \n21 Manipur 74 33 9 116 \n22 Meghalaya 3 0 1 4 \n23 Mizoram 23 5 0 28 \n24 Nagaland 0 1 0 1 \n25 Odisha 45 9 2 56 \n26 Puducherry 3 3 0 6 \n27 Punjab 129 76 1 206 \n28 Rajasthan 53 40 1 94 \n29 Sikkim 2 0 0 2 \n30 Tamil Nadu 82 82 11 175 \n31 Telangana 47 32 1 80 \n32 Tripura 8 2 0 10 \n33 Uttar Pradesh 106 66 6 178 \n34 Uttarakhand 26 16 1 43 \n35 West Bengal 69 47 5 121 \nTOTAL 1821 1027 116 2964 \n\nPage 4 of 4 \nANNEXURE - II \nState/UT-wise details of athletes supported under Sports Promotional Schemes of SAI \n \nS. No. State/UT 2017-2018 2018-2019 2019-2020 2020-2021 2021-2022 \n    Boys Girls Total Boys Girls Total Boys Girls Total Boys Girls Total Boys Girls Total \n1 Andhra Pradesh 180 84 264 125 58 183 93 50 143 89 35 124 73 28 101 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 69 43 112 149 83 232 63 43 106 98 69 167 93 58 151 \n3 A"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |328", "t": "Poultry, Sheep and Goat Rearing", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *328 \n \nANSWERED ON 21.12.2021 \n \nPromotion of Sports \n \n*328.     SHRI GIRISH CHANDRA: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) the details of the Centrally Sponsored Schemes being \nimplemented by the Government for the promotion of sports in the \ncountry;  \n(b) the funds allocated under these schemes during each of the \nlast three years and the current year, sports-wise; and \n(c) the details of the expenditure incurred on these schemes \nduring the said period, year-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR] \n \n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN  REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c ) OF THE  \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *328 FOR 21 /12/2021 \nREGARDING PROMOTION OF SPORTS  ASKED BY SHRI GIRISH \nCHANDRA. \n \n(a): Presently, no Centrally Sponsored Scheme is being implemented \nby the Department of Sports. However, the Department of Sports , \nthrough the following Central Sector Schemes,  supplements efforts of \nthe State/UT Governments for development and promotion of sports: (i)  \nKhelo India ; (ii) A ssistance to National Sports Federations ;  (iii)  \nSpecial Awards to Winners in International sports events and their \nCoaches; (iv) National Sports Awards, (v) Pension to Meritorious Sports \nPersons; (vi) Pandit Deendayal Upadhyay National Welfare Fund  for \nSportspersons; (vii) National Sports Development Fund; and (viii) \nSports training centres through Sports Authority of India (SAI). Details \nof these schemes are in the public domain on the websites of this \nMinistry and SAI.  \n \n(b) and (c) Details of funds allocated and expenditure incurred  under \nthe schemes mentioned in part (a) during each of the last three years \nand the current year are given at Annexure. The Department of Sports \ndoes not maintain sports-wise allocation of funds. \n \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b ) to (c) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *328 TO BE ANSWERED \nON 21.12.2021 REGARDING “PROMOTION OF SPORTS” ASKED BY SHRI GIRISH CHANDRA: \n \n \n \n \n \n(Rs. in crore)  \n2018-19  \n \n2019-20  \n \n2020-21 \n \n2021-22 \n(upto  08.12.2021) \nS.No.  Scheme  Allocation Actual Allocation Actual Allocation Actual Allocation Actual \n1.  Sports Authority of India  395.00  395.00  615.00  615.00 500.00 612.21 660.41 470.16 \n2.  Khelo India  500.09  342.24  578.00  575.52 328.77 338.06 657.71 375.44 \n3.  Assistance to National Sports \nFederation  245.13  243.63   \n300.85  \n300.85 132.00 128.62 280.00 85.47 \n4.  Special (Cash) Awards  31.00  30.94  62.00  61.54 16.00 15.99 38.00 33.11 \n5.  National Sports Awards  2.00  1.83  2.00  1.65 7.50 7.25 \n6.  Pension to Meritorious Sports persons  30.00  29.77  47.00  46.99 14.00 13.22 15.00 4.92 \n7.  \nPandit Deendayal Upadhyay National \nWelfare Fund for  \nSportspersons  \n1.80  1.00  \n2.00  1.00 2.00 2.00 2.00 0.00 \n8.  National Sports Development Fund  2.00  2.00  77.15  77.15 7.23 7.23 25.00 0.00 \n Total   1207.02 1046.41  1684.00  1679.7 1007.5 1124.58 1678.12 969.10 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |329", "t": "Preservation of Siri Cow Breed", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF IDNIA\n \nMINISTRY O1F AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *329\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 21\nst\n \nDECEMBER, 2021\n \n \nSUBSIDY FOR AGRICULTURAL EXPORTS\n \n \n*329. \n \nSHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA\n \nVISWANATH:\n \nSHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY:\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government extends sops or\n \nconcessions under transport and \nmarketing scheme for\n \nagri exports, through mandis and at purchase centres;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and the results thereof, Stat\ne\n-\nwise;\n \nand\n \n \n(c) \n \nif not, the time by which such a scheme is\n \nproposed to be announced for the \ncountry including\n \nAndhra Pradesh and Telangana?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n(\na) to (c)\n:\n \n \nA statement is laid on the table of the House.\n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRE\nD TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n329\n \nFOR ANSWER ON \n21\n.12\n.2021\n \nBY \nSHRIMATI VANGA \nGEETHA \nVISWANATH & \nSHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY\n \nREGARDING \n“\nSUBSID\nY FOR AGRICULTURAL EXPORTS\n”\n.\n \n \n(a) \nto \n(\nc\n)\n:\n \n  \nAs per the information received from Ministry of Commerce & Industry, \nGovernment has brought out a Central Sector Scheme\n-\n \n“Transport and Marketing \nAssistance\n \n(TMA)\n \nfor Specified Agriculture Products”\n-\n \nfor providi\nng assistance for the \ninternational component of freight and marketing of agricultural produce, which is likely to \nmitigate disadvantage of higher cost of transportation of export of specified agriculture \nproducts due to trans\n-\nshipment and to promote brand\n \nrecognition for Indian agricultural \nproducts in the specified overseas markets. Initially the Scheme was available for exports \neffected from 1.03.2019 to 31.03.2020 and was later extended for the exports effected up \nto 31.03.2021.Further continuation of t\nhe Scheme, for the exports effected up to \n31.12.2023, has been approved with some modifications to the scheme.\n \n \n \n \nPromotion of \nagricultural exports is a continuous process\n. \nAgricultural and \nProcessed Food Products Export Development Authority (APEDA)\n \nprovi\ndes assistance to \nits registered exporters and other stakeholders under Market Development component of \nits scheme \"Agriculture & Processed Foods E\nxport Promotion Scheme” of APEDA\n. Under \nthe scheme component, assistance is \nalso \nprovided for participation i\nn buyer\n-\nseller \nmeets, trade delegations, international trade fairs/exhibitions etc. Assistance is also \nprovided for new product/ market development through conducting feasibility studies, trial \nshipments, and registration of brands abroad. \nUnder this compo\nnent, assistance \nupto \n50% of the total cost subject to a ceiling of Rs. 10 lakhs per study per beneficiary\n \nis \navailable\n.\n \nfurther, the a\nssistance will be upto 75% of the total cost subject to a ceiling of \nRs. 10 lakhs per study per beneficiary if conducted\n \nby\n \nTrade Associations/\n \nIndian \nmissions\n  \n \nabroad/ \n \nCentral / state Govt. agencies/ exporters\n \n \nbelonging to North \n-\n \nEastern \n \n\n \n \n \nStates, difficult\n \nareas namely\n \nHimalayan and land locked states, Island    Union \nTerritories, SC/ST \nand women beneficiaries\n. \nFor act\nivities initiated by APEDA the funding \nshall be 100%\n. \nAPEDA\n \n \nalso disseminates trade data and market intelligence to its \nregistered exporters. Steps have also be taken to develop packaging standards and \ntransport protocols for specific products/ markets.\n \n \n \n \nDepartment of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare is implementing Mission for \nIntegrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) under which financial assistance is \nprovided for various horticulture activities including \npost harvest management activities \nwherein su\nbsidy is provided for the purchase of \nRefrigerated Transport vehicles\n \nthrough \nState Governments. The component is demand/ entrepreneur\n-\ndriven from among \nentrepreneurs, private companies, cooperatives, farmers groups etc through commercial \nventures for whic\nh assistance at the rate of 35% of admissible project cost in general \nareas and 50% in hilly and scheduled area is available as credit linked back ended \nsubsidy.\n \n \n \n \nGovernment ha\nd\n \nalso \nintroduced Kisan Rail trains to enable speedy movement of \nperishables i\nncluding fruits, vegetables, meat, poultry, fishery and dairy products from \nproduction or surplus regions to consumption or deficient regions. \nKisan Rail enables \nfarmers to utilize the vast railway network to gain access to distant, bigger and more \nlucrati\nve markets. Since the launch of first Kisan Rail service on 7\nth\n \nAugust, 2020 and \nupto 28\nth\n \nNovember, 2021, Indian Railways have operated approximately 1,642 Kisan \nRail services. \nThe State wise breakup of Kisan Rail trains is at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n. \n \n \n \n \nFurther,"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |33", "t": "Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan", "head": "������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n����������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�\n������������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n����������������������� �\n��������������������������� �\n���������������������������������� �\n����������������������������� �\n��������������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n����������������������������������� �\n�����������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������\n���� �������� ������ ���� �������� �������� �������� ���� ���� ����������� ��� ��������� ���\n��������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������