uced in Assam between 2011 anil2O21, year-wise and if so, the details\nthereof;\n\n-2-\n(b): Total quantity of Rice produced in Assam [etween 2O11 and 2021 is\nas under:\nKMS Rice Production (in LMT)\n2011-12 45.{6\n2(,12!.13 51.29\n2013t-14 49.27\n2(,14t15 52.23\n20{ si-r 6 51.25\n2f)1Gi-17 47.27\n2017',-14 52.84\n2(J18i-19 52.21\n2fJ19t-20 49.85\n52.5rt\n2021,22* 41.87\n* As per First Advance Estimates of Production of rice during 2021-22,\npubtished by Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare.\nThe details of food grains sold by farmers to non-Government entities\nis not maintained by Government of lndia/FGl. \n'\n(d): The number of paddy purchase centres operated in Assam during\nKMS2O2O-21 and XMS 2021-22 is as unden-\nKMS FCI State\nGovt./Agencies\nTotal\n2A20-21 46 ,!35\n95\n142\n2021-22 (for Kharif crop) loo {95\n(e): Apart from locally procured rice, the food-grains distributed through\nPDS in Assam are dispatched from other procuring regions viz Punjab,\nHaryana, Uttar Pradesh, etc.\n(O and (g): A Tripartite Memorandum of Understanding {MOU) has been\nsigned among FG!, Government of Assam and Government of lndia for\nprocurement of rice under centralized Procurement (Non-DCP mode). The\nNon.DGP States are persuaded to take up Decentratized Procurement\n(DGP) Operations for procurement of wheat/rice,.\n*****\n2020821\n(c): State-wise details of paddy procured and MSP paid from K.MA 20fl-12\nto KMS 2421-22 is at AnnexureJ.\n\nEI\np\nllllal!:lr:'.r1.:\nIP\nEE\n3\nq\na9\nntEl 3\n3\np\nea\nti r\n, r,rg ;r'.r,\n't:.tti.':,r,1\nrE.\ncg\nE\nE\np\n; I3\n:\n6\nf 3\nE\n: a\n?\nE E\nT\nH\nH\nt3\nIIT\nEI\nH\nII\nH\nH\nI\nII\nH\nut\nI\nT\nt\nHtl!t\nI\nI\nH\nEI\nu\n?a\nII\nLa\nI\nIT\nH\nI\ne\no\n:\nP\n=\n;=\n.ld\nz2\n;<9U\n5r\nai\no3oo\n9=\ni6\no?\no\nZ\ne"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |644", "t": "Improvement in Railway Infrastructure", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 644 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 01.12.2021 \n \nIMPROVEMENT IN RAILWAY INFRASTRUCTURE \n   \n644.  SHRI BHOLANATH (B.P. SAROJ): \n         SHRI RAVNEET SINGH BITTU: \n       \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has any proposal to allow private \nplayers to lay tracks and collect revenues in the country; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with any possible additional \nburden on the railway commuters due to this new policy; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to introduce new \ntechnologies and financial models for improving the railway \ninfrastructure in the country; \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e)  if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) and (b): Ministry of Railways (MoR) has formulated a Participative \nPolicy, 2012 to encourage the investment in developing rail \nconnectivity by associating strategic partners and other investors. \nThe policy defines five Public Private Partnership models viz. Non -\nGovernment Railway (NGR), Joint Venture (JV), Customer Funded, \nBuild Operate Transfer (BOT) and BOT -annuity models. State \nGovernments/Local bodies/PSUs may also participate as stakeholder \nfor the development of new lines/gauge conversion project under the  \nCont....2/- \n\n-:2:- \nparticipative policy of MoR. In all such Public Private Partnership \n(PPP) Projects, train operation and revenue collection continues to \nremain with Railway. However, such entities get a share of revenue in \nlieu of owing/maintaining the infr astructure. The PPP mode has been \nfound to be quite successful in Railways, especially in providing last \nmile rail connectivity to many ports and industrial clusters. Since the \ntrain operation & tariff determination continues to remain with \nRailways no additional burden on railway commuters are incurred.  \n \nSo far, 14 projects of ` 9,234 Crore have already been completed \nthrough PPP mode. 10 more projects of  ` 19,417 Crore  are under \nimplementation including coal connectivity and port connectivity \nprojects and in addition, 7 more projects of ` 13,971 Crore have \nalready been granted In -Principle approval, which are under \ndevelopment stage. \n \n (c) to (e): The process of Moderni zation and introduction of new \ntechnologies are continuous process in Indian Railways. Adoption of \nmodern technologies covers various facets of railway working, which \nprimarily aimed at improving the operational efficiency and safety in \nRailway workings. The modern technology mainly  include \nintroduction of higher horse power locomotives, modernisation of \nSignaling and telecommunication system, improving the  capacity of \nwagons and coaches, station development, introduction of increased \nuse of IT -enabled se rvices for improved customer interface,  new \ntechnologies in improving the life -cycle  and reliability of  railway \nassets. All possible funding mechanisms are explored for \nmodernization of railway systems and introduction of new \ntechnologies, which are met  through both from Budgetary and Extra \nBudgetary Resources (EBR). \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |645", "t": "CCTV in Trains and Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.645 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 01.12.2021 \nCCTV IN TRAINS AND STATIONS \n  \n645. SHRIMATI MANEKA SANJAY GANDHI  \n  \n       Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether  the Ministry has installed CCTV cameras in all the \ncoaches of the trains in the country and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) whether CCTV cameras have been installed in all the railway \nstations in the country and if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) whethe r there has been a fall in the incidences of crimes in \nrailway since the installation of CCTV cameras?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND ELECTRONICS & \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) Ministry of Railways have approved works for installation of \nClosed Circuit Television (CCTV) Cameras in all train coaches \nincluding EMUs and passenger trains. CCTV Cameras have already \nbeen provided in 4934 coaches. Zone -wise details are appended as \nAppendix-I. \n \n(b) Indian Railways have ap proved works for provision of CCTV \nCamera at all stations except halt stations. So far, CCTV Cameras \nhave been installed at total 838 stations. Zone -wise details are \nappended as Appendix-II. \n \n \n\n \n(c) Policing on Railways being a State subject, prevention of crime, \nregistration of cases, their investigation and maintenance of law & \norder in Railway premises as well as on running trains are the \nstatutory responsibility of the State Governments, which they \ndischarge through Government Railway Police (GRP)/Distri ct Police.  \nHowever, Railway Protection Force (RPF) supplements the efforts of \nGRP to provide better protection and security of passenger are a & \npassengers.  Cases of Indian Penal Code (IPC) crimes are registered \nand investigated by the concerned Government Railway Police.  \n \nAs per data provided by GRP, the incidence of crime on Railways \nshows a decreasing trend during last three years from 2018 to 2020. \n \n***** \n \n\nAPPENDIX-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.645 BY SHRIMATI MANEKA \nSANJAY GANDHI TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n01.12.2021 REGARDING  CCTV IN TRAINS AND STATIONS \n \n(a) Railway zone -wise List of CCTV cameras in coaches is as \nfollows:- \nZONAL RAILWAY \nNO. OF CCTV \nCAMERAS IN \nCOACHES \nCENTRAL 384 \nEAST COAST 386 \nEAST CENTRAL 225 \nEASTERN 226 \nNORTH CENTRAL 125 \nNORTH EASTERN 106 \nNORTHEAST FRONTIER 97 \nNORTHERN 468 \nNORTH WESTERN 107 \nSOUTH CENTRAL 489 \nSOUTH EAST CENTRAL 144 \nSOUTH EASTERN 175 \nSOUTHERN 429 \nSOUTH WESTERN 344 \nWEST CENTRAL 83 \nWESTERN 1104 \nKONKAN 42 \nTotal 4934 \n \n*****  \n\nAPPENDIX-II REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.645 BY SHRIMATI MANEKA \nSANJAY GANDHI TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n01.12.2021 REGARDING CCTV IN TRAINS AND STATIONS \n(a) Railway Zone -wise List of CCTV cameras at stations is as \nfollows:- \nZONAL RAILWAY NO. OF CCTV CAMERAS \nAT STATIONS \nCENTRAL 112 \nEASTERN 27 \nEAST CENTRAL 55 \nEAST COAST 19 \nNORTHERN 93 \nNORTH CENTRAL 29 \nNORTH EASTERN 25 \nNORTHEAST FRONTIER 40 \nNORTH WESTERN 32 \nSOUTHERN 58 \nSOUTH CENTRAL 57 \nSOUTH EASTERN 52 \nSOUTH EAST CENTRAL 26 \nSOUTH WESTERN 22 \nWESTERN 65 \nWEST CENTRAL 26 \nMETRO 33 \nKONKAN 67 \nTOTAL 838 \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |646", "t": "New Railway Line in Assam", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 646 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 01.12.2021 \n \nNEW RAILWAY LINE IN ASSAM \n \n646. SHRI TOPON KUMAR GOGOI: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways is planning for new railway line in Assam \nfrom Hilghat to Golaghat and Sivasagar to Jorhat; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (c):   Salona (near Silghat) to Khumtai (near Golaghat) new line \nproject (99 km) has been included in Budget subject to requisite \nGovernment approvals. Final Location Survey (FLS) of this new line \nproject has been completed  and preparation of Detailed Project Report \n(DPR) is at advanced stage. \n \n Sivasagar to Jorhat new line project (62 km) has been included in \nBudget subject to requisite Government approvals. Final Location \nSurvey (FLS) of this new line project has been comp leted and \npreparation of Detailed Project Report (DPR) is at advanced stage. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |647", "t": "Free of Cost Food", "head": "ORIGIiIAL IN HIl{DI\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMIN|STRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLTC DISTRIBUTION\nDEPARTIUENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED OUESTION NO.647\nTO BE ANSWERED (,1{ {sr DECEMBER,2O21\nFREE OF COST FOOD\nWII! the Minister of CONSUilER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIG\nDISTRIBUTIoN rclttftr rrr&, vrc-u st{ sr6lrfr6. frd{ur d* be pteased to\nstate:\n(a) whether the Government is implementing any scheme for the\ndistributlon of free of cost food to lowincome group;\n(c) the time by which the said scheme is likely to be implemented in the\ncountry including Bundelkhand?\nAilSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT AilD\nGONSUMER AFFATRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n(sADHVr NIRANJAN JYOTI)\n(a) to (c): Yes Sir, to ameliorate the hardships faced by poor due to\neconomic disruption caused by Gorona virus and to ensure that no poor\nfamily suffers on account of non-availability of foodgrain due to disruptlon\nduring this pandemic, under Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yoina\n(PMGI(AY), Govt of lndia has made allocation of foodgrains @ 5 kg per\npenron per month free of cost for around 8O crore beneficiaries of all the 36\nStates/UTs (including Bundelkhand) covered under NFSA (Antyodaya Anna\nYolana (AAY) & Priority Househotds(PHH)) including those covered under\nDirect Benefit Transfer (DBT) for a period of I months i.e April-November'\n2O20 and again similarly during the period May .November, 202{. This\nscheme has been extended for a further period of four months i'e.\nDecember, 2021 to Matcht2022.\nt647. SHRI r(UNWAR PUSHPENDRA STNGH GHANDEL:\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |648", "t": "Online Learning", "head": "1 \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS   \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 648 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 1ST DECEMBER, 2021 \n \nONLINE LEARNING \n \n648.  SHRI ANUMULA REVANTH REDDY:  \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware that during the COVID -19 lockdown rural students in \nthe areas located on the foot of hillocks in the state of Telangana faced severe problems in online \nlearning mainly due to the non -availability of sufficient internet and mobile bandwidth in rural \nareas  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; and  \n \n(c)  whether the Government is taking any steps to designate internet service s bandwidth as \nan essential service to ensure that both BSNL and private telecom service providers provide \nsufficient bandwidth and stable internet in rural areas in the country including in the state of \nTelangana and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR COMMUNICATIONS  \n(SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN) \n \n(a) & (b)  A comprehensive initiative called PM eVIDYA  has been initiated as part \nof Atma  Nirbhar Bharat Abhiyaan on 17th May, 2020, which unifies all efforts related to \ndigital/online/on-air education to enable multi-mode access to education. The initiative includes:  \n DIKSHA (one nation, one digital platform) is the nation’s digital infrastruc ture for \nproviding quality e -content for school education in states/UTs and QR coded \nEnergized Textbooks for all grades are available on it. \n One earmarked Swayam  Prabha TV channel per class from 1 to 12 (one class, one \nchannel). \n Extensive use of Radio, Community radio and CBSE Podcast- Shiksha Vani. \n Special e-content for visually and hearing impaired developed on Digitally Accessible \nInformation System (DAISY) and in sign language on NIOS website/ YouTube. \nAll these schemes/programmes are available to all the students across the nation. \nTo reach out to those students who lack access to technology various innovative activities \nare being done at national, state or district level such as Gali -Gali Sim -Sim, Tili -Mili \nprogramme, Motor Eskool, Roving Teacher, Proj ect SMILE (Social Media Interface for \nLearning Engagement), e-Kaksha, formation of Whatsap p and other social media groups, Work \nBook Distribution at home, Teacher calling to maintain connects with students. \n \nAlso, Internet access under BHARATNET scheme has  been made available to \nGovernment institutions and to improve the internet connectivity in rural areas the CSC e -\nGovernance Services India Ltd (CSC -SPV) of MEITY has been assigned the task of providing \nFibre to the Home (FTTH) connectivity to the Government Institutions, including schools. \n \n(c)  No, Sir. No such proposal is under consideration of the Government. \n******** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |649", "t": "National Railway Station Development Corporation", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No.649 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 01.12.2021 \n \nNATIONAL RAILWAY STATION DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION \n649.   SHRI RAJIV RANJAN SINGH ALIAS LALAN SINGH: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has closed the National Railway Station \nDevelopment Corporation; \n(b) if so, the likely effect on the projects which has been undertaken \nby this corporation; \n(c) the details of the number of stations given to them for \ndevelopment and the current status thereof; and \n(d) the details of funds allocated and spent on such projects? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n(a) and (b): Yes, Sir.  Government has given ‘in principle’ approval for \nclosure of Indian Railway Stations Development Corporation (IRSDC).  \nThe projects undertaken by IRSDC shall be handed over to respective \nZonal Railways and Rail Land Development Authori ty (RLDA).  Zonal \nRailways and RLDA will further develop the station projects. \n(c) and (d): IRSDC was undertaking techno -economic feasibility \nstudies for 63 stations across the country.  Rani Kamlapati  Railway \nStation and Gandhinagar Capital (Gujarat) Railway Station have been \ncommissioned and rest of the stations are at various stages of \nstudies/ development. Rani Kamlapati Railway Station has been \ndeveloped through Public Private Partnership with no cost to \nRailways and Gandhinagar Capital (Gujarat) Railway Station has been \ndeveloped through equity participation of Government of Gujarat and \nMinistry of Railways. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |65", "t": "Faculty Position in CEIs", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 65 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \nFaculty Position in CEIs \n65.  SHRI S. VENKATESAN:      \n���������������������EDUCATION�����������������������\n� ���� ���� ������� ��� ��������� �������� ������ ��������� ���� �������������� ����\n���������������������������������������\n� �������� �������� ������������������������������� ����� ������ ������������ ������ ����� ���\n����� �������� ������������ ������������� ������ ���������� ��� ���� ����������� ��� ���� ��������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������\n� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������\n� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������\n�\n        ANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n             (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n���� ���� ������� ��� ��������� �������� ������ ������������� ������ ���� ��������� �����������\n���������������� ���� ����������� �������� ������������ ������������ ������������� ��������\n������ ���� ��������������