enditure incurred from the fund. \n***** \n  \n  \n \n  \n  \n\nAnnexure referred to in part (a) & (b) of reply to Unstarred Question No – 663 \nState wise details of the allocation of DMF fund along with the details of the schemes \n  \nS.No. Sectorwise \nwork \nAndhra Pradesh Assam** Bihar$ Chhattisgarh Gujarat \nNo. \nof  Projects \nAmount \nSpent \n (in cr) \nNo. \nof  Projects \nAmount \nSpent  \n(in cr) \nNo. \nof  Projects \nAmount \nSpent  \n(in cr) \nNo. \nof  Projects \nAmount \nSpent \n (in cr) \nNo. \nof  Projects \nAmount \nSpent \n(in cr) \nHigh Priority work-\n60%  \n                    \n1 Drinking water \nsupply  \n2665 68.25 31 4.21 3 0.06 6143 335.41 1916 31.21 \n2 Environment \nPreservation \n& pollution \ncontrol \nmeasures \n6 0.00 6 0.52 5 1.60 1111 119.72 419 2.70 \n3 Health  977 151.43 18 2.79 38 1.97 3951 633.85 1367 30.93 \n4 Education  2612 37.14 64 3.34 12 0.62 11691 1237.28 5879 126.64 \n5 Welfare of \nWomen and \nChildren \n1376 15.20 22 0.18 18 0.81 3762 251.47 2215 54.02 \n6 Welfare of \naged and \ndisabled \npeople \n4 0.12 2 0.69 1 0.08 235 35.71 25 0.11 \n7 Skill \ndevelopment  \n92 0.45 17 3.60 0 0.00 1197 145.77 970 48.20 \n8 Sanitation 436 5.44 9 0.22 4 0.03 1439 140.23 756 10.84 \n9 Other 0 0.00 0 0.00 0 0.00 9753 798.20 0 0.00 \nSub Total 8168 278.03 169 15.55 81 5.17 39282 3697.65 13547 304.64 \nOther Priority \nwork-40% \n                    \n1 Physical \ninfrastructure  \n6562 122.76 66 11.66 5 0.51 12253 1208.38 2749 75.62 \n2 Irrigation 82 3.58 3 0.37 0 0.00 981 116.61 170 8.48 \n3 Energy and \nwatershed \ndevelopment \n20 0.85 5 0.51 1 0.00 2676 238.66 378 6.93 \n4 Any other \nmeasures for \nenhancing \nenvironmental \nquality  \n0 0.00 2 0.17 1 0.01 0 0.00 115 1.30 \n5 Other 48 3.40 11 0.00 8 0.59 732 87.89 0 0.00 \nSub Total 6712 130.60 87 12.70 15 1.11 16642 1651.54 3412 92.33 \nTotal 14880 408.63 256 28.26 96 6.28 55924 5349.19 16959 396.97 \n  \nS.No. Sectorwise \nwork \nHimachal Pradesh$ Jharkhand$ Karnataka Jamm