l\n \n295\n \n262\n \n282.46\n \n24.\n \nDepartmental\n \n-\n \n-\n \n0.07\n \n \n \nTOTAL\n \n1947\n \n1236\n \n3336.47\n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |747", "t": "Projects for the development of Minorities", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 747 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2021 \n  \nPROJECTS FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF MINORITIES \n  \n747. SHRI RAJU BISTA: \n            \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of works undertaken by the Government for the development of \nminorities; and \n(b) the status and the details of works under which assistance has been provided \nto minority communities in Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts during the last five \nyears? \n \nA N S W E R \n  \nMINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI)  \n[  \n(a)   The Government is implementing various schemes for the welfare and \nupliftment of every section of the society including minorities specially \neconomically weaker and down trodden sections all over the country with \nschemes like Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (PMJAY), Pradhan Mantri \nMudra Yojana (PMMY), Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM KISAN), \nPradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY), Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY), \nBeti Bachao Beti Padhao Yojana, etc. Ministry of Minority Affairs also implements \nprogrammes/ schemes for socio-economic and educational empowerment of the \nsix (6) centrally notified minority communities namely Sikhs, Budhists, Christians, \nParsis, Muslims and Jains through its Educational Empowerment schemes, Skill \nDevelopment schemes and Infrastructure Development schemes. \n \nUnder Infrastructure Development, the Ministry implements Pradhan Mantri Jan \nVikas Karyakram (PMJVK), a Centrally Sponsored Scheme and is now \nimplemented in 1300 identified Minority Concentration Areas (MCAs) of the \ncountry with the objective to develop socio-economic assets and basis amenities \nin these areas. The areas covered under PMJVK have been increased from 90 \nDistricts originally to 308 Districts in 33 States/ UTs. The MCAs include 109 \nMinority Concentration District Headquarters (MCD Hqrs) added for the first time, \n\n870 Minority Concentration Blocks (MCBs) and 321 Minority Concentration \nTowns (MCTs). The MCAs have been identified on the basis of concentration of \nminority population, and backwardness in terms of socio-economic or basic \namenity parameters as compared to national average.  \n  \nSince 2014-15, under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas Karyakram,  an amount of \nRs. 70565 lakh (till 30.11.2021) has been spent for various projects which include \n42 Degree Colleges, 177 Residential Schools, 1552 School Buildings, 23,464 \nAdditional Class Rooms/ACR Blocks, 14,312 Teaching Aid & Smart Classes, 681 \nHostels, 23 Working Women Hostels, 97 ITI Buildings, 13 Polytechnics, 19 Skill \nCentres, 2049 Health Centres & Other Health Projects, 1 Unani Medical College, \n18630 Drinking Water Supply Projects, 6041 Anganwadi Centres, 409 Sadhbhav \nMandaps, 167 Common Service Centres, 574 Market Sheds, 9 Hunar Hubs, \n5455 Sanitation–Toilet projects, 76 Sports Facilities, etc have been approved/ \nconstructed in Minority Concentrated Areas. All sections of the society, living in \nthese areas benefit from these infrastructure projects.  \n \n(b) The Ministry has, since inception of the Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas Karyakram \n(PMJVK) Scheme, approved the various projects amounting to Rs. 445338 lakh \nin West Bengal, which include 18833-Additional Class Rooms (ACRs), 107- ACR \nBlocks, 234-School Buildings, 14790- Anganwadi Centres, 170005- Cybergram, \n5000- Solar Lanterns, 21665 Drinking Water Projects, 1314 Health related \nprojects, 340-Hostels, 73519- Houses under Indira Awas Yojana (IAY), 37-ITI \nBuildings, 188 – Market Shed, 08-Polytechnics, 151-Sadbhav Mandaps, 3578-\nToilets, 479-Teaching Aid and Smart Class Rooms, 01-Working Women Hostel, \n59490-Skill Training and 04-Skill Centres, etc.  \n \n During the last five years, the Ministry under PMJVK scheme approved \nvarious projects amounting to Rs.2691.01 lakh in Darjeeling District which \ninclude 63 Additional Class Rooms, 89 Anganwadi Centres, 5 Hostels, 7 \nSadbhav Mandap and 1 Working Women Hostel. The Ministry has also approved \nvarious project amounting to Rs.837.72 lakh in Kalimpong District, which include \n4 Health Related Projects, 2 Hostels and 1 School Building. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |748", "t": "Target Capacity of PMAY-U", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 748 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 02, 2021 \n \nTARGET CAPACITY OF PMAY-U \n \nNO. 748.   SHRI SANJAY KAKA PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state:- \n \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to make provision of new fund to increase target \ncapacity of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojna (PMAY) and if so, the details thereof; \n(b)  the details of funds proposed by the Union Governme nt under PMAY, district-wise; \nand \n(c) the details of houses build under PMAY-Urban an d rural scheme which is audited by \nCentral Government authority? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a):   No, Sir. \n  \n(b): States/ Union Territories (UTs)-wise and distr ict-wise details of houses sanctioned \nunder Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY-U) along wit h Central assistance approved \nthereof are given at Annexure. \n \n(c): Under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY-U), par ticipating States/ Union Territories \n(UTs) have undertaken demand survey for assessing a ctual demand of housing in urban \nareas and reported a demand of 112.24 lakh houses. Against this, a total of 114.06 lakh \nhouses have been sanctioned so far involving Central assistance of  ₹ 1,84,808.00 crore; \n