rprises set up under Prime \nMinister‘s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) in the Satara district of \nMaharashtra during th\ne last three years; \n \n(b) \n \nwhether there are any plans to expand the programme with some additional \nsubsidies and encouragements; \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) \n \nif not, the reasons there\nfor?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRI\nSES\n \n(\nSHRI NARAYAN RANE\n)\n \n \n(a):\n \nDetails of new micro units set up under Prime Minister’s Employment \nGeneration Programme (PMEGP) in the Satara district of Maharashtra during the last \nthree years are given below:\n \n \n \nYear\n \nNo. of new \nPMEGP units set \nup \n \nMargin Money \nSubsidy disbursed \n \n(Rs. in lakh)\n \nEstimated Employment \nGenerated \n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n188\n \n537.32\n \n1504\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n122\n \n356.29\n \n976\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n111\n \n363.77\n \n888\n \n \n(b) to (d):\n \nMinistry of MSME has also introduced further financial assistance \nunder PMEGP in the form of second loan of up to Rs. 1.00 crore with subsidy of 15% \nof the project cost (20% for NER and Hill areas) for expansion/upgradation of the \nexisting PMEGP\nREGP\n/\n/\nMUDRA\n \nunits from the year 2018\n-\n19. Further improvements \nin the scheme are made from time to time.\n \n \n****\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |815", "t": "Progress under Saubhagya", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.815 \nANSWERED ON 02.12.2021 \n \nPROGRESS UNDER SAUBHAGYA \n815. SHRI ARUN SAO: \n \n Will the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of progress of Pradhan Mantri Sahaj Bijli Har Ghar Yojana- \n(Saubhagya), State-wise; \n \n(b) the total number of beneficiaries under Saubhagya Scheme in Chhattisgarh, \ndistrict-wise including Bilaspur, Mungeli and Gaurela-Pendra- Marwahi; \n \n(c) the number of families yet to be given the benefits as on date; and \n \n(d) the details of funds allocated and expenditure incurred during the last three years \nand the current year under Saubhagya, year-wise? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF POWER AND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY  \n \n(SHRI  R.K. SINGH) \n \n(a) The Government of India had launched Pradhan Mantri Sahaj Bijli Har Ghar Yojana – \nSaubhagya in October, 2017 with the objective of achieving universal household \nelectrification. The scheme entailed providing electricity connections to all un -electrified \nhouseholds in rural areas and all poor households in urban a reas in the country. Under the \nSaubhagya scheme, as on 31.03.2021 all the States have reported 100% electrification of \nall the willing un -electrified households, identified before 31.03.2019. As reported by the \nStates, 2.817 crore households have been electrified since the launch of Saubhagya, up to \n31.03.2021. State-wise details are as per Annexure – I. \n \n(b) District-wise details of the total number of Beneficiaries under the Saubhagya \nScheme in Chhattisgarh, including Bilaspur, Mungeli and Gaurela –Pendra Marwahi are as \nper Annexure – II. \n \n(c) The State of Chhattisgarh has reported that there are no households that are yet to \nbe given the benefits under Saubhagya Scheme as on date. \n \n(d) Year-wise details of funds allocated and Funds released to the States during the \nlast three years and the current year under Saubhagya are as per Annexure – III. \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \n ANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS ( a) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 815 \nANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON 02.12.2021 \n   \nStates- UTs -wise electrification of households since launch of Saubhagya Scheme \nSl.No. Name of the States/ UTs No of Households \nelectrified from \n11.10.2017 to \n31.03.2019 \nNo of Households \n(identified before \n31.03.2019) \nelectrified from  \n01.04.2019 to \n31.03.2021 \nTotal HHs \nelectrified as on \n31.03.2021 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 1,81,930 0 1,81,930 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 47,089 0 47,089