ubarnagiri-\nSrirampur Road from \n8/000 Km to 17/000 Km \n& from 24/500 Km to \n30/000 Km \n14.50 3632.00 42.73 \n20"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|7|UNSTARRED |858", "t": "Four-laning Road Projects in Assam", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 858 \n ANSWERED ON 2ND DECEMBER, 2021 \nFOUR-LANING ROAD PROJECTS IN ASSAM \n858. SHRI TOPON KUMAR GOGOI : \n        Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क  परिवहन  औि  िाजमार्ग  मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Government is aware of the slow construction work on the \nfour-laning project in Assam and if so, the details thereof; \n(b)   the measures being taken to speed up the said construction work; and \n(c)  whether the Government is aware that the said condition of the existing \nroad is very pathetic and if so, the measures being taken to repair the \nsame? \n \nANSWER \n THE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n(a)  Yes Sir. The details of on -going 4 laning projects in Assam is at \nAnnexure-A. \n(b)     The measures taken by the Government to speed up the construction \nwork are: \n(i)       Expediting the progress of pre -construction activities such as \nLand Ac quisition, Utility Shifting, Forest Clearance/Wildlife \nClearances, etc. by continuous liasoning with the State/District \nAdministration is being done by Higher Authorities of NHIDCL at HQ \nlevel and also at field level by Regional Office/PMU/Site Offices. \n\n(ii) Review meetings/Video Conferencing are being held regularly with \nContractors/Field Officers by Higher Authorities of NHIDCL to \nexpedite the progress of projects. District Administration is also \nmonitoring the progress of projects from time to time. \n(iii)  Notice to the contractors has been issued from time to time as \nper provisions of Contract Agreement to expedite the progress of \nprojects. \n(iv)  Actions are being taken against Non -performing contractors by \nduly terminating the projects for  poor progress  and simultaneously \nfresh contracts are being awarded.           \n(c)   To maintain traffic worthiness of the affected stretches, the roads are \nbeing  maintained through the contractor or at their risk and cost as per \nthe contract provision. \n\nAnnexure-A \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 858 FOR \n02.12.2021 ASKED BY SHRI TOPON KUMAR GOGOI REGARDING FOUR -LANING ROAD PROJECTS IN \nASSAM. \n \nSl. \nNo Scheme Name of Project \nNH \nOld/ \nNew. \nLength  \n(Km) \nDate of \nSanction \nSanctioned \nCost Rs. Cr\nore \nDate of S\ntart \nPhysical \nprogress \n(%) \nTarget dat\ne of compl\netion as pe\nr contract \nLikely date \nof completi\non \nReasons f\nor Delay \n1 SARDP-N\nE \n4-Laning of NH-37 f\nrom Nagaon By -pa\nss to Teliagaon  (k\nm 278.600 to km 2\n88.600) in the stat\ne of Assam under S\nARDP-NE Phase-A o\nn EPC mode -(Pack\nage-1) \n37/ \n127 \n10 \n14.01.16 225.02 \n01.07.20 54.29 31.12.21 31.03.2022 -- \n  \n2 SARDP-N\nE \n4-Laning of NH-37 f\nrom Teliagaon to \nRangagara (km 28\n8.600 to km 297.00\n0) in the state of A\nssam under SARDP-\nNE Phase-A on EPC \nmode – (Package – \n2) \n37/ \n127 \n8.4 01.07.20 47.35 31.12.21 31.03.2022 -- \n3 SARDP-N\nE \n4 laning from Rang\nagara to Kaliabhor \nTiniali from km 29\n7.00 to km 315.315 \nof NH-37 on EPC ba\nsis \n37/ \n127 \n18.315 12.01.16 289.99 23.10.17 53.05 21.04.20 31.03.2022 \nLA Issues, \nCash Flow \nProblem o\nf EPC Con\ntractor \n4 SARDP-N\nE \n4 laning from Kalia\nbor Tinali to Dolab\nari section from K\nm 0.0 to Km 17.3 o\nf NH 37-A including \nconstruction of ne\nw Brahmaputra bri\ndge \n37A/ \n715 \n17.30 31.10.14 811.28 29.11.14 87.62 28.11.18 31.03.2022 \nTechnical \nProblem i\nn P-18&P-\n19 locatio\nn, LA Issu\nes \n5 SARDP-N\nE \n4 - lane highway co\nnnecting km 17.3 o\nf NH 37A and km 1\n82 of NH 52 betwe\nen Dolabari and Ja\nmuguri on EPC bas\nis \n37A & \n52 16.862 \